msgstr "对用同一组边界划分的分组调用 ``kivi.stability.csi_table`` ，自 0.6.0 起"

msgid "``VintagePd``"
msgstr "``VintagePd``"

msgid "``kivi.vintage.vintage_table`` on a loan panel, from 0.6.0"
msgstr "对贷款面板数据调用 ``kivi.vintage.vintage_table`` ，自 0.6.0 起"

msgid "``Dataset.bank_data()``"
msgstr "``Dataset.bank_data()``"

msgid "Unchanged; ``kivi.datasets.load_bank()`` returns the same data from 0.6.0"
msgstr "不变；自 0.6.0 起 ``kivi.datasets.load_bank()`` 返回相同的数据"

msgid "Binning and WOE"
msgstr "分箱与 WOE"

msgid ""
"DistanceBins and FrequencyBins previously calculated group assignments and statistics together. "
"Use bin_edges with uniform or quantile, call pandas.cut, then pass the groups to woe_table. Codes"
" listed in abnormal_vals become the special argument: pass them to bin_edges, and use "
"kivi.binning.cut with the same codes in place of pandas.cut. CategoryBins users can pass the "
"label series directly."
msgstr ""
"旧版 DistanceBins 和 FrequencyBins 在同一步骤中完成分箱和统计。现在先用 bin_edges 选择 uniform 或 quantile，再用 pandas.cut "
"分组，最后将结果传给 woe_table。abnormal_vals 中的编码改由 special 参数指定：传给 bin_edges，并用带相同编码的 kivi.binning.cut 代替 "
"pandas.cut。原 CategoryBins 用户可直接传入类别标签序列。"

msgid ""
"Version 0.5.0 adds woe_transform in place of WOEScore. WOEScore matched raw values against the "
"min_bin and max_bin columns of a WOE table. Form the groups with the development edges instead, "
"then pass them to woe_transform with the woe_table result. A value that matches no group raises "
"an error, as WOEScore did with error=\"error\"; pass unseen to choose its WOE instead."
msgstr ""
"0.5.0 新增 woe_transform，取代 WOEScore。旧版 WOEScore 把原始取值与 WOE 表中的 min_bin 和 max_bin "
"列逐一比对。现在请改用开发样本的边界划分分组，再把分组和 woe_table 的结果一起传给 woe_transform。与 WOEScore 设置 error=\"error\" "
"时一样，匹配不到任何分组的取值会引发错误；也可以传入 unseen 指定其 WOE。"

msgid ""
"Version 0.4.0 adds ``chimerge_edges`` and ``tree_edges`` in place of ``Chi2Bins`` and "
"``TreeBins``. They are new implementations rather than ports, so the edges can differ. "
"``Chi2Bins`` started from 10 quantile bins, tested at a 0.9 confidence level, added 0.5 to every "
"expected count and kept at least three bins; ``chimerge_edges(values, target, alpha=0.1, "
"initial_bins=10)`` comes closest. ``TreeBins`` reported the midpoints that scikit-learn chooses "
"as thresholds, while ``tree_edges`` reports the largest observed value below each cut. Compare "
"the edges on a fixed reference sample before switching."
msgstr ""
"0.4.0 新增 ``chimerge_edges`` 和 ``tree_edges``，用来替代 ``Chi2Bins`` 和 "
"``TreeBins``。它们是重新实现而非移植，因此边界可能不同。``Chi2Bins`` 从 10 个等频箱开始，在 0.9 置信水平下检验，给每个期望计数加 "
"0.5，并至少保留三个箱；最接近的写法是 ``chimerge_edges(values, target, alpha=0.1, initial_bins=10)``。``TreeBins`` "
"报告 scikit-learn 选出的中点阈值，而 ``tree_edges`` 报告每个切分点下方的最大观测值。切换之前，请在固定的基准样本上核对边界。"

msgid ""
"Codes listed in ``abnormal_vals`` of ``Chi2Bins`` and ``TreeBins`` become the ``special`` "
"argument of ``chimerge_edges`` and ``tree_edges``. As before, the codes and their labels are left"
" out of the fit; pass the same codes to ``kivi.binning.cut`` to give each one its own group."
msgstr ""
"``Chi2Bins`` 和 ``TreeBins`` 的 ``abnormal_vals`` 中列出的编码，对应 ``chimerge_edges`` 和 ``tree_edges`` 的 "
"``special`` 参数。与以前一样，这些编码连同其标签不参与拟合；把相同的编码传给 ``kivi.binning.cut`` ，即可让每个编码单独成组。"

msgid ""
"For PSI.fit(), form both sets of groups using the same reference edges, then call psi_table. It "
"returns raw counts and a contribution per bin. Previously the psi column repeated the overall "
"total. The new smoothing rule preserves counts and normalizes each distribution after replacing "
"zeros. Recheck thresholds when migrating saved analyses."
msgstr ""
"迁移 PSI.fit() 时，先用同一组基准边界划分两期样本，再调用 psi_table。新结果包含各组的真实计数和单组贡献；旧结果在 psi "
"列逐行重复总值。新的平滑口径会在补零后归一化。迁移历史分析时应重新核对阈值。"

msgid "Models, scorecards and calibration"
msgstr "模型、评分卡与校准"

msgid ""
"These modules are new implementations, so compare their output with the legacy code on a fixed "
"reference sample before switching."
msgstr "这些模块都是重新实现的，切换之前请先在固定的参考样本上与旧版代码的结果对比。"

msgid ""
"The legacy ``lift`` column was cumulative. In ``gains_table``, ``lift`` is the lift of each band "
"and ``cum_lift`` the cumulative lift. The metrics take a score that rises with risk, such as a "
"PD; pass ``-score`` for scorecard points. ``ModelEvaluate`` rescaled each sample by its own "
"minimum and maximum, so its scores were not comparable across samples; the new functions use the "
"scores as given."
msgstr ""
"旧版的 ``lift`` 列是累计值。在 ``gains_table`` 中， ``lift`` 是每个分数段的提升， ``cum_lift`` 才是累计提升。这些指标要求分数随风险升高，例如 "
"PD；评分卡分值请传入 ``-score`` 。 ``ModelEvaluate`` 会用每个样本自己的最小值和最大值重新缩放分数，导致不同样本间的分数不可比；新函数直接使用传入的分数。"

msgid ""
"``VIF`` called statsmodels without a constant, which measures uncentred R²; ``vif`` includes an "
"intercept in every auxiliary regression, as in the textbook definition, so the values differ. "
"``stepwise`` replaces ``StepWise`` and by default keeps every coefficient positive, as WOE inputs"
" require. ``logistic_regression`` fits the model in NumPy, so statsmodels is no longer needed."
msgstr ""
"``VIF`` 调用 statsmodels 时没有加常数项，衡量的是未中心化的 R²； ``vif`` 按教科书定义在每个辅助回归中都包含截距，因此数值会不同。 ``stepwise`` 取代"
" ``StepWise`` ，默认保证所有系数为正，这正是 WOE 输入的要求。 ``logistic_regression`` 用 NumPy 拟合模型，不再需要 statsmodels。"

msgid ""
"``BaseScoreAndPDO`` took bad:good odds, for example ``odds=1/50``. ``base_odds`` is good:bad, so "
"pass ``base_odds=50``; passing ``1/50`` silently gives an offset of 712.9. The legacy "
"``PDToScore`` divided by ln 2 only in one of its branches; ``pd_to_score`` and ``score_to_pd`` "
"are exact inverses."
msgstr ""
"``BaseScoreAndPDO`` 接收的是坏好比，例如 ``odds=1/50`` 。 ``base_odds`` 是好坏比，因此应传入 ``base_odds=50`` ；若传入 "
"``1/50`` ，会在没有任何提示的情况下得到 712.9 的偏移量。旧版 ``PDToScore`` 只在其中一个分支里除以了 ln 2； ``pd_to_score`` 和 "
"``score_to_pd`` 互为精确的反函数。"

msgid ""
"``get_omega`` becomes ``prior_correction`` for probabilities and ``corrected_intercept`` for the "
"model intercept."
msgstr "``get_omega`` 的功能由 ``prior_correction`` （校正概率）和 ``corrected_intercept`` （校正模型截距）取代。"

msgid "Not yet ported"
msgstr "尚未迁移的功能"

msgid ""
"Sample weights, variable selection, scorecards, model evaluation and calibration arrive in 0.5.0."
" CSI, vintage analysis and strategy tools are planned. Spark, SQL, AHP, model wrappers and "
"application code remain in the historical revisions."
msgstr "样本权重、变量筛选、评分卡、模型评估和校准从 0.5.0 起提供。CSI、账龄分析和策略工具已在计划中。Spark、SQL、AHP、模型封装和应用代码仍保留在历史版本中。"

msgid "Portfolio analysis and production binning"
msgstr "资产组合分析与生产环境分箱"

msgid ""
"Version 0.6.0 replaces three more legacy classes. They are new implementations as well, so "
"compare their output with the legacy code on a fixed reference sample before switching."
msgstr "0.6.0 版又替代了三个旧版类。它们同样是重新实现的，切换之前请先在固定的参考样本上与旧版代码的结果对比。"

msgid ""
"``WOEBatch`` fitted the WOE of many columns at once, and ``ManualBinsTool`` merged bins by hand "
"afterwards. ``fit_spec`` fits every column with the binning function chosen for it, and its "
"``BinningSpec`` saves the edges and WOE tables as versioned JSON. Nothing is re-binned "
"automatically: to merge bins by hand, pass the merged edges for that column in ``bins``."
msgstr ""
"``WOEBatch`` 一次拟合多列的 WOE， ``ManualBinsTool`` 随后手动合并分箱。 ``fit_spec`` 用为每列选定的分箱函数拟合各列，得到的 "
"``BinningSpec`` 把边界和 WOE 表保存为带版本号的 JSON。它不会自动重新分箱：要手动合并分箱，请在 ``bins`` 中为该列传入合并后的边界。"

msgid ""
"``CSI`` matched the points to the bins by position and lost the missing group. ``csi_table`` "
"matches the points to the groups by label, keeps the missing group, and raises for an observed "
"group without points unless ``unseen_points`` gives them. Its contributions sum to the change of "
"the variable's average points."
msgstr ""
"``CSI`` 按位置把分值对应到各箱，并丢失了缺失值分组。 ``csi_table`` 按标签把分值对应到各组，保留缺失值分组；若某个出现的分组没有分值，除非用 "
"``unseen_points`` 给出，否则会报错。各组贡献之和等于该变量平均分值的变化。"

msgid ""
"``VintagePd`` built the vintage table from repayment schedules and observation dates. "
"``vintage_table`` takes a long panel with one row per loan and month on book and a bad flag that "
"you define, for example ``status == \"90+\"``. Pass ``weights=amount`` for the amount-weighted "
"rates of ``VintagePd``. Months that a cohort has not reached are NaN rather than 0."
msgstr ""
"``VintagePd`` 根据还款计划和观察日期构建 vintage 表。 ``vintage_table`` 接受长格式的面板数据，每笔贷款每个账龄月一行，并由你自行定义坏账标记，例如 "
"``status == \"90+\"`` 。传入 ``weights=amount`` 即可得到 ``VintagePd`` 按金额加权的比率。批次尚未达到的账龄月为 NaN 而不是 0。"

msgid ""
"``bin_edges`` fits numeric bin edges on a reference sample and returns them as an array for "
"``pandas.cut``. The reference can be a list, a NumPy array or a pandas Series. Keep the array: "
"the same edges must be applied to every sample that is compared with the reference."
msgstr ""
"``bin_edges`` 在基准样本上拟合数值分箱边界，并以数组形式返回，供 ``pandas.cut`` 使用。基准样本可以是列表、NumPy 数组或 pandas "
"Series。请保存这个数组：与基准样本比较的每个样本都必须使用同一组边界。"

msgid ""
"In credit scoring, binning is the classing step of scorecard development: a continuous variable "
"becomes a handful of groups whose WOE can be read, explained to the business and monitored over "
"time. This page compares the ways to choose the edges."
msgstr "在信用评分中，分箱是评分卡开发的变量分组环节：连续变量被划分为少数几组，每组的 WOE 都可以解读、向业务解释并持续监控。本页比较选择边界的几种方式。"

msgid "Quantile and uniform edges"
msgstr "等频与等距边界"

msgid ""
"Use quantile bins to divide the reference observations by rank, or uniform bins to divide their "
"numeric range into equal widths."
msgstr "等频分箱按基准样本中的秩划分观测，等距分箱按取值范围等宽划分。"

msgid ""
"Quantile bins hold roughly equal numbers of observations, which suits skewed variables. Uniform "
"bins keep equal widths, so a long tail can leave some bins nearly empty."
msgstr "等频分箱中各箱的观测数大致相同，适合偏态变量。等距分箱保持宽度一致，长尾可能让部分箱几乎为空。"

msgid ""
"Account balances are typical of financial data: most customers hold small amounts and a few hold "
"very large ones. On the bank data, quantile bins split the reference sample evenly, while uniform"
" bins put almost everyone into the first bin."
msgstr "账户余额是典型的金融数据：大多数客户余额不高，少数客户余额极大。在银行数据上，等频分箱把基准样本均匀切开，而等距分箱几乎把所有人都放进第一个箱。"

msgid ""
"Histogram of account balance with quantile and uniform edges, and the number of customers in each"
" bin for both methods"
msgstr "账户余额的直方图及等频、等距边界，以及两种方法下每箱的客户数"

msgid ""
"Left: the balance distribution, cut at its 99th percentile, with the quantile edges (solid) and "
"the first uniform edge (dashed). Right: customers per bin. Uniform bins leave the upper bins "
"almost empty, so their WOE would rest on a handful of customers."
msgstr "左图：余额分布（截断于第 99 百分位），实线为等频边界，虚线为第一个等距边界。右图：每箱的客户数。等距分箱让高位的箱几乎为空，这些箱的 WOE 只能依赖极少数客户。"

msgid "Custom edges and special values"
msgstr "自定义边界与特殊值"

msgid ""
"The edges do not have to come from ``bin_edges``. Any increasing array works with ``pandas.cut`` "
"and the metric functions, so policy bands and expert edges fit the same workflow. Keep infinite "
"outer edges so that every future value is covered."
msgstr ""
"边界不一定来自 ``bin_edges``。任何递增数组都可以传给 ``pandas.cut`` "
"和指标函数，因此政策分段和专家边界也能用于同一流程。请保留两端的无穷边界，确保之后的任何取值都有归属。"

#, python-format
msgid ""
"Risk data often encode a state as a number, for example -1 for \"never contacted\" or 999 for "
"\"no record\". In the bank data, 82% of the reference customers have ``pdays == -1``, so quantile"
" binning collapses the variable into a single bin and its information value is lost. An edge at "
"-1 gives the code a bin of its own."
msgstr ""
"风控数据常用数字编码某种状态，例如用 -1 表示“从未联系”，用 999 表示“无记录”。在银行数据中，82% 的基准样本客户 ``pdays == "
"-1``，因此等频分箱会把该变量压缩成一个箱，信息值随之丢失。在 -1 处设置边界，可以让这个编码单独成箱。"

msgid "WOE by age band and by days since the previous contact"
msgstr "按年龄分段和距上次联系天数计算的 WOE"

msgid ""
"Left: age bands show a U shape, with the youngest and oldest customers more likely to subscribe. "
"Right: customers contacted in a previous campaign within 200 days stand out once the -1 code has "
"its own bin."
msgstr "左图：年龄分段呈 U 形，最年轻和最年长的客户更可能认购。右图：-1 编码单独成箱后，200 天内在上一轮营销中被联系过的客户明显突出。"

msgid ""
"The edge at -1 works because no real value of ``pdays`` lies below the code. To fit the other "
"edges from the data instead, or for a code inside the range of real values, pass the code in "
"``special``; see :ref:`special-values`."
msgstr ""
"在 -1 处设边界之所以可行，是因为 ``pdays`` 的真实取值都不小于这个编码。如果想让其余边界由数据拟合，或者编码落在真实取值的范围之内，请把编码传给 ``special`` ，见 "
":ref:`special-values` 。"

msgid "Merging fine bins"
msgstr "合并细分箱"

msgid ""
"Scorecard development usually starts from many fine bins and merges neighbours, a step known as "
"coarse classing, until each bin is large enough to be stable and the WOE follows a trend that can"
" be explained. Select a subset of the fitted edges to merge bins; keeping the first and last edge"
" keeps the infinite ends."
msgstr ""
"评分卡开发通常先做较多的细分箱，再合并相邻的箱（即粗分箱），直到每箱样本足够稳定，WOE "
"也呈现可以解释的趋势。从已拟合的边界中选取一部分即可合并分箱；保留第一个和最后一个边界，就保留了两端的无穷边界。"

msgid "WOE of ten fine balance bins next to WOE of three merged bins"
msgstr "余额 10 个细分箱与合并后 3 个箱的 WOE 对比"

msgid ""
"Ten fine bins (left) zigzag; three merged bins (right) rise steadily with balance and give up "
"little information value."
msgstr "10 个细分箱（左）呈锯齿状；合并后的 3 个箱（右）随余额稳步上升，信息值损失很小。"

msgid ""
"Choosing the merges by hand works for a few variables. The supervised methods in the next section"
" search for them automatically, and two of them start from fine quantile bins in the same way."
msgstr "变量不多时，可以手工选择合并方式。下一节的有监督方法会自动搜索合并方案，其中两种同样从等频细分箱出发。"

msgid "Supervised binning"
msgstr "有监督分箱"

msgid ""
"Quantile and uniform edges ignore the target. The supervised methods use it to place edges "
"between customers with different event rates, which is what the WOE of each bin measures. They "
"take the values and a 0/1 target, as Series on the same index or as arrays and lists matched by "
"position, omit missing values and any codes passed in ``special`` while fitting, and return edges"
" in the same form as ``bin_edges``: increasing, with infinite outer edges, ready for "
"``pandas.cut``, ``woe_table`` and ``psi_table``. Each returns at most ``max_bins`` bins, 5 by "
"default."
msgstr ""
"等频与等距边界不考虑目标变量。有监督方法则利用目标变量，把边界放在事件率不同的客户之间，而这正是每箱 WOE 所度量的差异。它们接收数值和 0/1 目标变量：二者是 Series "
"时须索引相同，是数组或列表时按位置对应；拟合时忽略缺失值以及传给 ``special`` 的编码，返回的边界与 ``bin_edges`` 形式相同：严格递增、两端为无穷，可直接用于 "
"``pandas.cut``、``woe_table`` 和 ``psi_table``。每种方法最多返回 ``max_bins`` 个箱，默认为 5。"

msgid "Function"
msgstr "函数"

msgid "How it fits the edges"
msgstr "拟合边界的方式"

msgid "Main options"
msgstr "主要参数"

msgid "``chimerge_edges``"
msgstr "``chimerge_edges``"

msgid "Merges adjacent fine bins whose event rates do not differ significantly."
msgstr "合并事件率没有显著差异的相邻细分箱。"

msgid "``max_bins``, ``alpha``"
msgstr "``max_bins``、``alpha``"

msgid "``tree_edges``"
msgstr "``tree_edges``"

msgid "Splits the values where a decision tree gains the most purity."
msgstr "在决策树纯度提升最大的位置切分数值。"

msgid "``max_bins``, ``min_bin_share``, ``criterion``"
msgstr "``max_bins``、``min_bin_share``、``criterion``"

msgid "``monotonic_edges``"
msgstr "``monotonic_edges``"

msgid "Merges adjacent fine bins until the WOE rises or falls steadily."
msgstr "合并相邻细分箱，直到 WOE 稳定上升或下降。"

msgid "``max_bins``, ``direction``"
msgstr "``max_bins``、``direction``"

msgid ""
"As with ``bin_edges``, fit the edges on the reference sample only and apply the saved array to "
"every other sample."
msgstr "与 ``bin_edges`` 一样，只在基准样本上拟合边界，再把保存的数组用于其他所有样本。"

msgid "ChiMerge"
msgstr "ChiMerge（卡方分箱）"

msgid ""
"``chimerge_edges`` starts from fine quantile bins, 20 by default, and repeatedly merges the "
"adjacent pair whose event rates are most alike, the pair with the smallest chi-square statistic. "
"Merging continues while more than ``max_bins`` bins remain or while some adjacent pair does not "
"differ significantly at level ``alpha``."
msgstr ""
"``chimerge_edges`` 从等频细分箱（默认 20 个）开始，反复合并事件率最接近、即卡方统计量最小的一对相邻箱。只要箱数仍多于 ``max_bins``，或仍有相邻两箱在显著性水平"
" ``alpha`` 下差异不显著，就继续合并。"

msgid ""
"Five bins were allowed, but with five and with four bins some adjacent pair still had a chi-"
"square below 3.84, the critical value at ``alpha=0.05``, so merging went on to three bins. Pass "
"``alpha=None`` to merge down to ``max_bins`` only, or a larger ``alpha`` to keep more bins."
msgstr ""
"虽然允许 5 个箱，但在 5 箱和 4 箱时，仍有相邻两箱的卡方值低于 ``alpha=0.05`` 对应的临界值 3.84，因此继续合并到 3 个箱。传入 ``alpha=None`` "
"只合并到 ``max_bins`` 个箱；传入更大的 ``alpha`` 可保留更多箱。"

msgid ""
"Smallest chi-square between adjacent balance bins as ChiMerge merges them, and the WOE of the "
"three final bins"
msgstr "ChiMerge 合并余额分箱过程中相邻箱的最小卡方值，以及最终 3 个箱的 WOE"

msgid ""
"Left: the smallest chi-square between adjacent bins as the fine bins are merged, read from left "
"to right. Merging stops at the first count no larger than max_bins at which every pair lies above"
" the alpha line. Right: the WOE of the final bins rises with balance."
msgstr "左图：细分箱逐步合并时相邻箱之间的最小卡方值，从左向右阅读。当箱数不超过 max_bins 且所有相邻箱都位于 alpha 线上方时，合并停止。右图：最终各箱的 WOE 随余额上升。"

msgid "Decision tree"
msgstr "决策树"

msgid ""
"``tree_edges`` grows a decision tree on the one variable. Each split cuts a bin at the value that"
" most reduces the impurity of the target, measured by entropy (the default) or by the Gini index "
"with ``criterion=\"gini\"``. The bin whose best split gains the most is split next, until there "
"are ``max_bins`` bins or no allowed split reduces the impurity. ``min_bin_share`` keeps every bin"
" above a share of the observations, 5% by default, so that its WOE rests on enough customers. The"
" interior edges are observed values."
msgstr ""
"``tree_edges`` 在单个变量上生长一棵决策树。每次切分都选在使目标变量不纯度下降最多的取值处，不纯度默认用熵度量，传入 ``criterion=\"gini\"`` "
"则用基尼指数。最优切分收益最大的箱先被切分，直到箱数达到 ``max_bins``，或没有允许的切分能降低不纯度。``min_bin_share`` 要求每箱的观测占比不低于给定值（默认 "
"5%），使每箱的 WOE 建立在足够多的客户之上。内部边界都是观测值。"

msgid ""
"The tree separates the classes best, but it does not look for a trend: customers above 6,046 "
"subscribe less often than those just below them. A scorecard needs a WOE pattern that can be "
"explained, so check the trend of tree bins before using them, and merge bins where it breaks."
msgstr ""
"决策树对两类客户的区分最好，但它并不追求趋势：余额高于 6,046 的客户，认购比例反而低于余额略低于该值的客户。评分卡需要可以解释的 WOE "
"形态，因此使用决策树分箱前应检查趋势，并在趋势被打破处合并分箱。"

msgid "Entropy reduction of every possible first cut of balance, and the WOE of the five tree bins"
msgstr "余额每个可能的第一次切分带来的熵下降，以及决策树 5 个箱的 WOE"

msgid ""
"Left: the entropy reduction of every possible first cut. Cuts in the shaded areas would leave "
"less than min_bin_share of the customers in a bin. The dashed lines are the tree's cuts, numbered"
" in the order they were made. Right: the WOE of the five bins rises, then falls in the top bin."
msgstr ""
"左图：每个可能的第一次切分带来的熵下降。阴影区域内的切分会让某个箱的客户占比低于 min_bin_share。虚线是决策树的切分点，编号为切分的先后顺序。右图：5 个箱的 WOE "
"先上升，在最高的箱中回落。"

msgid "Monotonic binning"
msgstr "单调分箱"

msgid ""
"``monotonic_edges`` also starts from fine quantile bins. Whenever two adjacent bins break the "
"trend, it merges them and recomputes the WOE (pool adjacent violators), so the WOE of the final "
"bins is strictly increasing or strictly decreasing. If more than ``max_bins`` bins remain, it "
"then merges the most similar adjacent pairs by chi-square. ``direction=\"auto\"`` tries both "
"trends and keeps the one with the larger information value; pass ``\"increasing\"`` or "
"``\"decreasing\"`` to impose the trend that the business expects."
msgstr ""
"``monotonic_edges`` 同样从等频细分箱开始。每当相邻两箱违背趋势，就将它们合并并重新计算 WOE（合并相邻违序者，pool adjacent "
"violators），因此最终各箱的 WOE 严格递增或严格递减。若箱数仍多于 ``max_bins``，再按卡方统计量合并最相近的相邻箱。``direction=\"auto\"`` "
"会尝试两种趋势，保留信息值较大的一种；传入 ``\"increasing\"`` 或 ``\"decreasing\"`` 可以指定业务预期的趋势。"

msgid ""
"The trend is checked with the same smoothing as ``woe_table``, so the WOE that ``woe_table`` "
"reports for these bins is monotonic as well, even when a bin has no events."
msgstr "趋势检查使用与 ``woe_table`` 相同的平滑规则，因此即使某个箱没有事件，``woe_table`` 对这些箱给出的 WOE 也是单调的。"

msgid "WOE of the fine balance bins with the pooled monotonic WOE, and the WOE of the five final bins"
msgstr "余额细分箱的 WOE 与合并后的单调 WOE，以及最终 5 个箱的 WOE"

msgid ""
"Left: the WOE of the fine quantile bins zigzags; pooling adjacent violators turns it into a "
"rising step (max_bins=None). Right: merged further to max_bins=5, the WOE still rises with "
"balance."
msgstr "左图：等频细分箱的 WOE 呈锯齿状；合并相邻违序箱后变为上升的阶梯（max_bins=None）。右图：进一步合并到 max_bins=5 后，WOE 仍随余额上升。"

msgid "Comparing the methods"
msgstr "方法对比"

msgid ""
"Supervised edges are chosen to separate the sample they are fitted on, so the information value "
"on that sample is optimistic. Compare the methods on a later sample as well, keeping the edges "
"fixed."
msgstr "有监督边界是为区分拟合样本而选出的，因此在该样本上算出的信息值偏乐观。保持边界不变，在之后的样本上也对比一次各方法。"

msgid ""
"On the reference sample all three supervised methods beat five quantile bins. On the later sample"
" they fall behind: much of the extra separation they found in balance was noise, which is common "
"for a weak variable and a few hundred events. Validate supervised edges on a later or held-out "
"sample before adopting them, and keep the variable under PSI monitoring once it is in use."
msgstr ""
"在基准样本上，三种有监督方法都优于 5 "
"个等频箱；在之后的样本上却落在后面：它们在余额上多找到的区分度，很大一部分是噪声。对于较弱的变量和仅有几百个事件的样本，这种情况很常见。采用有监督边界之前，应先在之后的样本或留出样本上验证；变量投入使用后，还要持续做"
" PSI 监控。"

msgid "Special codes"
msgstr "特殊编码"

msgid ""
"A code such as ``pdays == -1`` is fitted as an ordinary value unless it is passed in ``special``."
" Monotonic binning then puts the 2,475 reference customers coded -1, who were never contacted "
"before, into one bin with the 78 customers contacted within 96 days, the group most likely to "
"subscribe:"
msgstr ""
"像 ``pdays == -1`` 这样的编码，如果不传给 ``special`` ，就会被当作普通取值参与拟合。此时单调分箱会把基准样本中编码为 -1、此前从未被联系过的 2,475 "
"位客户，与 96 天内被联系过的 78 位客户放进同一个箱，而后者正是最可能认购的群体："

msgid ""
"With ``special=[-1]`` the code and its labels are left out of the fit, and ``cut`` with the same "
"code gives it a group of its own ahead of the intervals:"
msgstr "传入 ``special=[-1]`` 后，该编码连同其标签不参与拟合；再把同一编码传给 ``cut`` ，它就会单独成组，排在各区间之前："

msgid ""
"Fitted on the contacted customers alone, the WOE falls steadily: the more recent the previous "
"contact, the more likely a customer is to subscribe. ``max_bins`` and the trend apply to the "
"intervals only, so each special group comes on top of them with a WOE of its own. "
"``chimerge_edges`` and ``tree_edges`` take ``special`` in the same way, and ``min_bin_share`` "
"counts only the values that are fitted."
msgstr ""
"只用被联系过的客户拟合后，WOE 稳定下降：上一次联系越近，客户越可能认购。``max_bins`` 和单调趋势只约束各区间，每个特殊值组在此之外单独成组，并有自己的 "
"WOE。``chimerge_edges`` 和 ``tree_edges`` 以同样的方式接受 ``special`` ，``min_bin_share`` 也只统计参与拟合的取值。"

msgid "Ties and constant values"
msgstr "重复切点与常量"

msgid "Tied cut points are collapsed. A constant reference produces one bin."
msgstr "重复的切点会被合并。常量基准样本只产生一个箱。"

msgid ""
"The number of bins can therefore be smaller than requested, and ``bin_edges`` then issues a "
"``UserWarning``. A single value that covers much of the reference, such as a code for \"not "
"applicable\", often causes this. Pass that value in ``special``, as described in the next "
"section."
msgstr ""
"因此实际箱数可能少于期望箱数，此时 ``bin_edges`` 会发出 ``UserWarning`` "
"。某个取值（例如表示“不适用”的编码）在基准样本中占比很大时，常会出现这种情况。请按下一节的方法把该取值传给 ``special`` 。"

msgid "Special values"
msgstr "特殊值"

msgid ""
"Many credit variables use codes such as ``-1`` or ``-999`` for \"not applicable\" or \"no "
"record\". Such a code is not a measurement, so it should neither shape the edges nor share an "
"interval with real values. Pass the codes in ``special`` to ``bin_edges`` to leave them out of "
"the fit, and pass the same codes to ``kivi.binning.cut`` to give each one its own group."
msgstr ""
"许多信贷变量用 ``-1`` 或 ``-999`` 这样的编码表示“不适用”或“无记录”。这类编码不是测量值，既不应影响边界，也不应与真实取值共用一个区间。把这些编码传给 "
"``bin_edges`` 的 ``special`` 参数，拟合时会排除它们；再把同样的编码传给 ``kivi.binning.cut`` ，每个编码就会单独成组。"

#, python-format
msgid ""
"In the bundled data, ``pdays`` is ``-1`` for the 82% of customers who were not contacted in an "
"earlier campaign. Without ``special``, every quantile is tied at ``-1``: ``bin_edges`` returns a "
"single bin and warns that ``-1`` makes up 82% of the fitted values. With ``special=[-1]`` the "
"remaining values are divided into five bins:"
msgstr ""
"在随包数据中，82% 的客户此前未被联系过，他们的 ``pdays`` 为 ``-1`` 。不传 ``special`` 时，所有分位点都重合在 ``-1`` ： ``bin_edges`` "
"只返回一个箱，并警告 ``-1`` 占拟合取值的 82%。传入 ``special=[-1]`` 后，其余取值被分成五个箱："

msgid ""
"The single bin had an IV of zero; separating the code shows that ``pdays`` is informative. The "
"categories of the result are the special values in the order given, followed by the intervals, "
"and ``woe_table`` and ``psi_table`` list the rows in that order. Special values are matched by "
"equality, so ``-1`` and ``-1.0`` are the same code. Without ``special``, ``cut`` returns the same"
" result as ``pandas.cut``."
msgstr ""
"原来那唯一一个箱的 IV 为零；把编码单独分出来之后，可以看出 ``pdays`` 是有信息量的。结果的类别依次为按给定顺序排列的特殊值和各区间， ``woe_table`` 和 "
"``psi_table`` 也按这个顺序列出各行。特殊值按相等关系匹配，因此 ``-1`` 和 ``-1.0`` 视为同一个编码。不传 ``special`` 时， ``cut`` 的结果与 "
"``pandas.cut`` 相同。"

msgid "The supervised methods take ``special`` as well; see :ref:`supervised-special`."
msgstr "有监督分箱方法同样接受 ``special`` ，见 :ref:`supervised-special` 。"

msgid "Sample weights"
msgstr "样本权重"

msgid ""
"``bin_edges`` and the supervised methods take ``weights``, for example the inverse sampling rates"
" of a stratified development sample, so that quantile edges and bin counts describe the "
"population rather than the sample. Weighted quantiles use the inverted CDF, so every interior "
"edge is an observed value, while unweighted quantile edges interpolate between observations:"
msgstr ""
"``bin_edges`` 和监督分箱方法都接受 ``weights`` "
"，例如分层抽样开发样本中各观测抽样比例的倒数，使等频边界和每箱计数反映总体而不是样本。加权分位数采用逆累积分布（inverted "
"CDF），因此每个内部边界都是实际观测到的取值；不加权时，等频边界则在观测值之间线性插值："

msgid ""
"Observations with zero weight are left out; the supervised methods leave out their labels too. "
":doc:`woe_iv` shows the same weights in ``woe_table``."
msgstr "权重为零的观测会被排除，监督分箱方法同时排除其标签。 :doc:`woe_iv` 展示了在 ``woe_table`` 中使用同样的权重。"

msgid "Applying the edges"
msgstr "应用边界"

msgid ""
"Infinite endpoints cover finite future observations outside the training range. Use the saved "
"edges with pandas.cut on every sample."
msgstr "两端延伸至无穷，因此可覆盖后续超出训练范围的有限值。保存边界，再对每期数据调用 pandas.cut。"

msgid ""
"Intervals are closed on the right, so a value equal to an edge belongs to the lower bin. Pass "
"``labels=False`` to ``pandas.cut`` for integer bin numbers instead of intervals."
msgstr "区间为左开右闭，因此等于某个边界的值归入较低的箱。若要得到整数箱号而不是区间，可向 ``pandas.cut`` 传入 ``labels=False``。"

msgid "Missing values and categories"
msgstr "缺失值与类别"

msgid ""
"Missing reference values are ignored when the edges are fitted, and ``pandas.cut`` leaves them "
"missing. The metric functions then count them as a separate group."
msgstr "拟合边界时会忽略基准样本中的缺失值，``pandas.cut`` 也会保留缺失值。指标函数随后将它们计为单独的一组。"

msgid ""
"Pass categorical labels directly to the metric functions. A missing label is a separate group. "
"Only observed groups appear. Categorical groups, including the result of ``pandas.cut``, follow "
"the order of their categories with missing values last; other labels follow the order in which "
"they first appear. For WOE, group and target series must have identical indices; arrays and lists"
" are matched by position."
msgstr ""
"类别变量可直接传给指标函数。缺失标签独立成组。输出仅列出实际观测到的组。分类型分组（包括 ``pandas.cut`` 的结果）按类别顺序排列，缺失值排在最后；其他标签按首次出现的次序排列。计算"
" WOE 时，分组与标签序列的索引必须完全一致；数组和列表按位置对应。"

msgid "Invalid input"
msgstr "无效输入"

msgid "``bin_edges`` raises ``ValueError`` when:"
msgstr "以下情况下，``bin_edges`` 会抛出 ``ValueError``："

msgid "``bins`` is not a positive integer;"
msgstr "``bins`` 不是正整数；"

msgid "``method`` is neither ``\"quantile\"`` nor ``\"uniform\"``;"
msgstr "``method`` 既不是 ``\"quantile\"`` 也不是 ``\"uniform\"``；"

msgid "the reference values are not one-dimensional or not numeric;"
msgstr "基准样本的取值不是一维或不是数值；"

msgid "``special`` is not one-dimensional or contains a missing value;"
msgstr "``special`` 不是一维或含有缺失值；"

msgid ""
"the reference has no observations apart from missing and special values, or contains an infinite "
"value that is not special."
msgstr "除缺失值和特殊值外，基准样本没有观测值，或含有不属于特殊值的无穷值。"

msgid ""
"``chimerge_edges``, ``tree_edges`` and ``monotonic_edges`` raise ``ValueError`` for the same "
"problems with the values, for an option outside its range, and when:"
msgstr ""
"``chimerge_edges``、``tree_edges`` 和 ``monotonic_edges`` 在数值出现上述同样的问题、参数超出取值范围，以及以下情况下会抛出 "
"``ValueError``："

msgid "``values`` and ``target`` are Series without identical indices, or have different lengths;"
msgstr "``values`` 与 ``target`` 是索引不完全相同的 Series，或者长度不同；"

msgid "``target`` contains a label other than 0 and 1, or a missing label;"
msgstr "``target`` 含有 0 和 1 以外的标签，或含有缺失标签；"

msgid "the observed values, apart from special values, do not cover both classes."
msgstr "除特殊值外，非缺失数值对应的标签没有同时包含两个类别。"

msgid ""
"A PD model is calibrated when its probabilities match the default rates that are later observed. "
"Calibration is a separate question from ranking: a model can order applicants well and still "
"predict default rates that are too low for the whole portfolio. :mod:`kivi.calibration` corrects "
"probabilities for the sampling of the development data, summarizes the grades of a master scale "
"and tests them, and maps a score to probabilities with Platt scaling or isotonic regression."
msgstr ""
"如果 PD 模型给出的概率与之后观测到的违约率相符，就称模型是校准的。校准与排序是两个不同的问题：一个模型可以把申请人排得很好，却仍然对整个资产组合预测了过低的违约率。 "
":mod:`kivi.calibration` 针对开发数据的抽样方式校正概率，汇总主标尺的各个等级并对其进行检验，还能用 Platt 缩放或保序回归把评分映射为概率。"

msgid "Correcting for oversampling"
msgstr "过采样校正"

msgid ""
"Bad outcomes are often oversampled for development, for example to a sample with as many bads as "
"goods. The model then predicts probabilities for that sample, not for the portfolio. With the "
"development sample's event rate :math:`\\bar y` and the portfolio's event rate :math:`\\tau`, the"
" prior correction of King and Zeng multiplies the odds of every probability by"
msgstr ""
"开发模型时，常常对坏样本做过采样，例如使好坏样本数量相等。这样模型预测的是该样本上的概率，而不是资产组合上的概率。设开发样本的事件率为 :math:`\\bar y` ，资产组合的事件率为 "
":math:`\\tau` ，King 和 Zeng 的先验校正把每个概率的几率乘以"

#, python-format
msgid ""
"A model developed on a sample with 50% bads, for a portfolio with a 2% default rate, turns a "
"probability of 0.5 into 0.02:"
msgstr "如果模型在坏样本占 50% 的样本上开发，而资产组合的违约率为 2%，那么概率 0.5 会变为 0.02："

msgid ""
"The correction keeps the order of the probabilities. For a logistic regression it only shifts the"
" intercept by :math:`\\ln \\omega`, so the coefficients and the points per WOE in "
":doc:`scorecard` stay the same:"
msgstr "校正不改变概率的排序。对逻辑回归而言，它只是把截距平移 :math:`\\ln \\omega` ，因此系数以及 :doc:`scorecard` 中每单位 WOE 对应的分值都保持不变："

msgid "Grades of a master scale"
msgstr "主标尺的等级"

msgid ""
"A master scale divides the PD range into a fixed set of grades, so that ratings from different "
"models share one meaning. The examples below use the PDs of the scorecard from :doc:`scorecard` "
"on the development and monitoring samples:"
msgstr "主标尺把 PD 的取值范围划分为一组固定的等级，使不同模型给出的评级具有统一的含义。下面的示例使用 :doc:`scorecard` 中的评分卡在开发样本和监控样本上给出的 PD："

msgid ""
"Assign the grades with ``pandas.cut`` and the PD edges of the scale, then compare the observed "
"default rate of each grade with its mean predicted PD using ``calibration_table``. The intervals "
"are closed on the right, so a PD on an edge goes to the lower grade, and ``include_lowest=True`` "
"keeps a PD of exactly 0 in the first grade:"
msgstr ""
"用 ``pandas.cut`` 和标尺的 PD 边界划分等级，再用 ``calibration_table`` 比较每个等级的观测违约率与平均预测 PD。区间为左开右闭，因此恰好落在边界上的 "
"PD 归入较低的等级；``include_lowest=True`` 让恰好为 0 的 PD 留在第一个等级："

msgid ""
"``calibration_table`` accepts any grouping, such as score bands or deciles of the PD. It counts "
"the groups like ``woe_table``: categorical groups keep the order of their categories, and grades "
"without observations are left out."
msgstr "``calibration_table`` 接受任意分组，例如分数段或 PD 的十分位组。它的计数方式与 ``woe_table`` 相同：分类型分组保持类别顺序，没有观测值的等级会被略去。"

msgid "Testing each grade"
msgstr "逐个等级检验"

msgid ""
"Each grade is tested on its own against the hypothesis that its PD is not too low. Both tests are"
" one-sided: a small p-value means that the grade has more defaults than its PD predicts."
msgstr "每个等级单独检验，原假设是其 PD 没有偏低。两种检验都是单侧的：p 值较小，说明该等级的违约数多于其 PD 的预测。"

msgid ""
"The **binomial test** treats the :math:`N` obligors of a grade as independent, each defaulting "
"with probability :math:`p`. Its p-value is the probability of at least the observed :math:`d` "
"defaults, :math:`P(D \\ge d)`."
msgstr ""
"**二项检验** 把一个等级中的 :math:`N` 个债务人视为相互独立，每人以概率 :math:`p` 违约。其 p 值是至少出现观测到的 :math:`d` 次违约的概率，即 "
":math:`P(D \\ge d)` 。"

#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"The **Jeffreys test** starts from the Jeffreys prior :math:`\\mathrm{Beta}(1/2, 1/2)` for the "
"default rate. Its p-value is the posterior probability that the default rate is at most "
":math:`p`, the distribution function of :math:`\\mathrm{Beta}(d + 1/2, N - d + 1/2)` at "
":math:`p`. The European Central Bank asks for this test in the validation of PD models."
msgstr ""
"**Jeffreys 检验** 以 Jeffreys 先验 :math:`\\mathrm{Beta}(1/2, 1/2)` 作为违约率的先验分布。其 p 值是违约率不超过 :math:`p` "
"的后验概率，即 :math:`\\mathrm{Beta}(d + 1/2, N - d + 1/2)` 在 :math:`p` 处的分布函数值。欧洲央行在 PD 模型验证中要求使用这一检验。"

#, python-format
msgid ""
"No grade is rejected at the usual 5% level. To see the tests at work, scale the PDs down as if "
"the portfolio defaulted at 6% rather than at the 11.6% of the development sample. The monitoring "
"sample still defaults at the development rate, so the PDs are now too low:"
msgstr "在常用的 5% 水平下，没有等级被拒绝。为了观察检验的效果，把 PD 按资产组合违约率为 6%（而非开发样本的 11.6%）的情形调低。监控样本的违约率仍与开发样本相当，因此这些 PD 现在偏低："

msgid ""
"Observed default rate against mean predicted PD for each grade, for the original and the scaled-"
"down PDs"
msgstr "原始 PD 与下调后 PD 的各评级实际违约率对平均预测 PD"

msgid ""
"The grades of the original PDs lie close to the diagonal, while those of the scaled-down PDs lie "
"above it: more defaults than predicted. Larger points hold more customers."
msgstr "原始 PD 的各评级贴近对角线，而下调后 PD 的各评级位于对角线上方：违约多于预测。点越大，客户越多。"

msgid ""
"For the same counts, the Jeffreys p-value is always a little lower than the binomial one, so the "
"Jeffreys test rejects slightly more readily. Both tests assume independent defaults; defaults "
"that move together in a downturn make them reject more often than their nominal level."
msgstr "对相同的计数，Jeffreys 检验的 p 值总是略低于二项检验，因此 Jeffreys 检验稍微更容易拒绝。两种检验都假定违约相互独立；经济下行期违约同涨同落，会使它们的拒绝频率高于名义水平。"

msgid "Testing all grades at once"
msgstr "一次检验所有等级"

msgid ""
"The Hosmer-Lemeshow test adds up the squared differences between observed and predicted defaults "
"over all :math:`g` groups:"
msgstr "Hosmer-Lemeshow 检验把全部 :math:`g` 个分组中观测违约数与预测违约数之差的平方累加起来："

#, python-brace-format
msgid "H = \\sum_{k=1}^{g} \\frac{(d_k - n_k \\bar p_k)^2}{n_k \\bar p_k (1 - \\bar p_k)}."
msgstr "H = \\sum_{k=1}^{g} \\frac{(d_k - n_k \\bar p_k)^2}{n_k \\bar p_k (1 - \\bar p_k)}."

msgid ""
"On the sample the model was fitted on, form about ten groups of similar size from the sorted PDs "
"and compare :math:`H` with a chi-square distribution with :math:`g - 2` degrees of freedom, the "
"default:"
msgstr "在拟合模型所用的样本上，把排序后的 PD 分成约十个大小相近的组，并将 :math:`H` 与自由度为 :math:`g - 2` 的卡方分布比较，这也是默认设置："

msgid ""
"PDs that were not fitted on the tested sample, such as the grades of the monitoring sample, lose "
"no degrees of freedom, so pass ``ddof=0``:"
msgstr "如果 PD 不是在被检验的样本上拟合的（例如监控样本的各等级），自由度不会减少，因此传入 ``ddof=0`` ："

msgid "Concentration of the grades"
msgstr "等级的集中度"

msgid ""
"A master scale differentiates risk poorly when most obligors fall into a few grades. The "
"Herfindahl-Hirschman index sums the squared shares of the grades: it is :math:`1/k` when all "
":math:`k` grades are equally full and 1 when one grade holds everybody. With ``normalize=True`` "
"it runs from 0 to 1 instead:"
msgstr ""
"如果大多数债务人都落在少数几个等级，主标尺对风险的区分能力就较差。赫芬达尔-赫希曼指数是各等级占比的平方和： :math:`k` 个等级人数相同时为 :math:`1/k` "
"，所有人都在同一等级时为 1。设置 ``normalize=True`` 后，取值范围改为 0 到 1："

msgid ""
"``calibration_table`` leaves out empty grades. To count them, pass the counts of every grade of "
"the scale, for example ``grades.value_counts(sort=False)``."
msgstr "``calibration_table`` 会略去空等级。如需把空等级计算在内，请传入标尺上每个等级的计数，例如 ``grades.value_counts(sort=False)`` 。"

msgid "Calibrating a score"
msgstr "校准评分"

msgid ""
"A score that ranks applicants well need not be a probability, and the PDs of a model may need "
"recalibrating on recent data. ``kivi.calibration`` fits two common mappings from a score to "
"probabilities. Like ``bin_edges`` and ``cut``, each comes as a pair: the fit returns plain "
"numbers, fitted once on a calibration sample, and the predict function applies them to the scores"
" of any later sample."
msgstr ""
"能把申请人排好序的评分不一定是概率，模型的 PD 也可能需要在近期数据上重新校准。 ``kivi.calibration`` 拟合两种常用的从评分到概率的映射。与 ``bin_edges`` 和"
" ``cut`` 一样，每种映射都成对出现：拟合函数在校准样本上拟合一次并返回普通的数值，预测函数再把它们应用到之后任何样本的评分上。"

msgid "Platt scaling"
msgstr "Platt 缩放"

msgid "Platt scaling fits a logistic regression of the target on the score :math:`s`:"
msgstr "Platt 缩放以评分 :math:`s` 为自变量，对目标拟合逻辑回归："

#, python-brace-format
msgid "p(s) = \\frac{1}{1 + \\exp(-(a s + b))}."
msgstr "p(s) = \\frac{1}{1 + \\exp(-(a s + b))}."

#, python-format
msgid ""
"For a score that is already the log odds of a model, this is the logistic recalibration of Cox: a"
" slope of 1 and an intercept of 0 mean that the model is calibrated on the sample. Take the PDs "
"that were scaled down to a 6% default rate above. On the development sample, the fit keeps the "
"slope at 1 and raises the intercept by about 0.72, the log of the odds ratio that the correction "
"applied:"
msgstr ""
"如果评分本身就是某个模型的对数几率，这就是 Cox 的逻辑再校准：斜率为 1、截距为 0 说明模型在该样本上是校准的。以上文按 6% 违约率调低的 PD 为例。在开发样本上，拟合得到的斜率仍为 "
"1，截距则提高约 0.72，正是该校正所用优势比的对数："

msgid ""
"Apply the slope and intercept to the low PDs of the monitoring sample. The recalibrated grades "
"have the counts and rates of the grades of the original PDs again:"
msgstr "把斜率和截距应用到监控样本中偏低的 PD 上。再校准后的各等级，其计数和事件率又与原始 PD 的等级相同："

msgid ""
"The score need not be log odds. Platt scaling fits any score, and a score that falls as the risk "
"rises, such as scorecard points, gets a negative slope. When the score separates the classes, the"
" slope that maximizes the likelihood is infinite, and ``platt_fit`` raises "
":class:`kivi.selection.SeparationError`."
msgstr ""
"评分不必是对数几率。Platt 缩放适用于任何评分；风险越高评分越低的评分（例如评分卡分值）会得到负的斜率。当评分把两类完全分开时，使似然最大的斜率为无穷大， ``platt_fit`` 会引发"
" :class:`kivi.selection.SeparationError` 。"

msgid "Isotonic regression"
msgstr "保序回归"

msgid ""
"Isotonic regression assumes only that the event rate rises with the score. The pool-adjacent-"
"violators algorithm merges adjacent score bands until their event rates increase, and each band "
"gets its event rate. ``isotonic_fit`` returns the band edges, from ``-inf`` to ``inf`` like those"
" of ``bin_edges``, and the probability of each band:"
msgstr ""
"保序回归只假定事件率随评分上升。相邻违序合并算法不断合并相邻的评分段，直到各段的事件率递增，每段取其事件率。 ``isotonic_fit`` 返回分段边界（与 ``bin_edges`` "
"一样从 ``-inf`` 到 ``inf`` ）以及每个分段的概率："

msgid ""
"The bands are closed on the right, as in ``pandas.cut``, so they can also serve as grades. "
"``isotonic_predict`` gives each monitoring PD the probability of its band, and scores outside the"
" development range get the probability of the lowest or the highest band. A score that falls "
"between the observed scores of two bands gets the upper band; with ``increasing=False``, as for "
"scorecard points, that is the band with the lower risk:"
msgstr ""
"与 ``pandas.cut`` 一样，各分段为右闭区间，因此也可以用作等级。 ``isotonic_predict`` 给监控样本的每个 PD "
"赋予其所在分段的概率，超出开发样本范围的评分取最低或最高分段的概率。落在两个分段的观测评分之间的评分取上方的分段；若 ``increasing=False`` "
"（例如评分卡分值），这就是风险较低的分段："

msgid ""
"The step function follows the development sample closely, so some bands are small: the smallest "
"holds four customers of the monitoring sample. Fit isotonic regression on a large sample, and "
"check its bands on another sample as above. A band without events has a probability of 0, so "
"floor the probabilities where a PD of zero is not allowed."
msgstr ""
"阶梯函数紧贴开发样本，因此有些分段很小：最小的分段只有监控样本中的四位客户。请在大样本上拟合保序回归，并像上面那样在另一个样本上检查其分段。没有事件的分段概率为 0，因此在不允许 PD "
"为零的场合，请为概率设定下限。"

msgid "Weighted samples"
msgstr "加权样本"

msgid ""
"A development sample that keeps every bad but only some of the goods can be weighted back to the "
"portfolio, with each observation weighted by the inverse of its sampling rate. "
"``calibration_table``, ``platt_fit`` and ``isotonic_fit`` take such weights in ``weights``: "
"counts become sums of weights, and integer weights give the same result as repeating rows. The "
"binomial, Jeffreys and Hosmer-Lemeshow tests need whole numbers of observations and events, so "
"run them on an unweighted table."
msgstr ""
"保留全部坏样本、只保留部分好样本的开发样本，可以用每个观测抽样比例的倒数作为权重，加权还原到资产组合。 ``calibration_table`` 、 ``platt_fit`` 和 "
"``isotonic_fit`` 通过 ``weights`` 接受这样的权重：计数变为权重之和，整数权重与重复相应行的结果相同。二项检验、Jeffreys 检验和 Hosmer-"
"Lemeshow 检验需要整数的观测数和事件数，因此请在不加权的表上进行这些检验。"

msgid ""
":mod:`kivi.datasets` provides two kinds of example data: real bank marketing data with one row "
"per customer and a binary target, and a synthetic panel of loans with one row per loan and month."
msgstr ":mod:`kivi.datasets` 提供两类示例数据：真实的银行营销数据，每位客户一行，带二分类目标；以及合成的贷款面板数据，每笔贷款每个月一行。"

msgid "Bank marketing data"
msgstr "银行营销数据"

msgid ""
"``load_bank()`` loads 4,521 customers from the Bank Marketing data set. It has sixteen features "
"and an integer ``target``: 1 means that the customer subscribed to a term deposit."
msgstr "``load_bank()`` 读取 Bank Marketing 数据集中的 4,521 位客户。数据包含 16 个特征和整数标签 ``target`` ：1 表示客户认购了定期存款。"

msgid ""
"The examples in this documentation split the rows by position only to demonstrate two samples; "
"the split is not chronological. Earlier examples call ``Dataset.bank_data()``, which returns the "
"same data and keeps working."
msgstr "本文档中的示例按行的位置切分出两个样本，仅用于演示；这一切分不代表时间顺序。较早的示例调用 ``Dataset.bank_data()`` ，它返回相同的数据，并且可以继续使用。"

msgid "Synthetic loan panel"
msgstr "合成贷款面板"

msgid ""
"``make_loan_panel`` simulates the monthly history of a portfolio of instalment loans, for the "
"vintage and roll-rate analysis in :doc:`vintage`. The data is generated, not taken from a real "
"portfolio, and the same ``rng`` seed always gives the same panel:"
msgstr ""
"``make_loan_panel`` 模拟一个分期贷款资产组合的月度历史，供 :doc:`vintage` 中的 Vintage "
"分析和滚动率分析使用。数据是生成的，并非取自真实的资产组合；同一个 ``rng`` 种子总是给出同样的面板："

msgid ""
"The loans are spread at random over ``n_months`` origination months from January 2024, and each "
"loan has one row for every month end it is on book, up to the month after the last origination "
"month. The columns are:"
msgstr "贷款随机分布在从 2024 年 1 月开始的 ``n_months`` 个放款月中；每笔贷款在账上的每个月末都有一行，直到最后一个放款月的下一个月。各列如下："

msgid "Column"
msgstr "列"

msgid "Meaning"
msgstr "含义"

msgid "``loan_id``"
msgstr "``loan_id``"

msgid "Identifier of the loan, increasing with the origination month."
msgstr "贷款标识，随放款月份递增。"

msgid "``cohort``"
msgstr "``cohort``"

msgid "Origination month, a monthly ``pandas.Period``."
msgstr "放款月份，为月度 ``pandas.Period`` 。"

msgid "``month``"
msgstr "``month``"

msgid "Month of the observation, ``cohort + month_on_book``."
msgstr "观测所在月份，即 ``cohort + month_on_book`` 。"

msgid "``month_on_book``"
msgstr "``month_on_book``"

msgid "Months since origination, from 1."
msgstr "放款后经过的月数（账龄），从 1 开始。"

msgid "``term``"
msgstr "``term``"

msgid "Number of monthly instalments: 12, 24 or 36."
msgstr "月供期数：12、24 或 36。"

msgid "``amount``"
msgstr "``amount``"

msgid "Amount lent."
msgstr "放款金额。"

msgid "``balance``"
msgstr "``balance``"

msgid "Outstanding principal at the end of the month."
msgstr "月末的剩余本金。"

msgid "``status``"
msgstr "``status``"

msgid ""
"Days past due at the end of the month, an ordered categorical: ``current``, ``1-29``, ``30-59``, "
"``60-89`` and ``90+``."
msgstr "月末的逾期天数，为有序分类变量： ``current`` 、 ``1-29`` 、 ``30-59`` 、 ``60-89`` 和 ``90+`` 。"

msgid "How the panel is simulated"
msgstr "面板的模拟方式"

#, python-format
msgid ""
"Each loan is repaid in equal monthly instalments at 1% interest a month. Its status counts the "
"months since its oldest unpaid instalment fell due: one is ``1-29``, two ``30-59``, three "
"``60-89`` and four or more ``90+``. Within the term this is the number of instalments past due. "
"Every month:"
msgstr ""
"每笔贷款按月等额本息还款，月利率为 1%。其状态记录自最早一期未还期款到期以来的月数：一个月为 ``1-29`` ，两个月为 ``30-59`` ，三个月为 ``60-89`` ，四个月及以上为"
" ``90+`` 。在期限内，这就是逾期未还的期数。每个月："

msgid ""
"a current loan misses its instalment with a probability that peaks at its sixth month on book and"
" then declines, scaled by a risk factor of the loan and one of its cohort;"
msgstr "正常贷款漏缴当期期款的概率在账龄第六个月达到峰值，之后下降，并乘以该贷款和所在批次各自的风险系数；"

msgid ""
"a delinquent loan pays all its arrears and becomes current, pays one instalment and keeps its "
"status, or pays nothing and rolls to the next bucket, also after its term, and the later the "
"bucket, the less likely it cures and the more likely it rolls;"
msgstr "逾期贷款要么还清全部欠款、回到正常，要么只还一期、保持原状态，要么完全不还、滚动到下一个档位（期限结束后也是如此）；档位越靠后，回到正常的可能越小，滚动的可能越大；"

msgid "a ``90+`` loan pays nothing more, so its status and balance stay the same."
msgstr "``90+`` 的贷款不再还款，因此其状态和余额保持不变。"

msgid ""
"A loan leaves the panel in the month it pays its last instalment, which can come after its term "
"if it was behind. Loans are not charged off or prepaid."
msgstr "贷款在还清最后一期的当月离开面板；如果曾经逾期，这可能发生在期限之后。贷款不会被核销，也不会提前还款。"

msgid "Dataset and attribution"
msgstr "示例数据和署名"

msgid ""
"Bank Marketing by S. Moro, P. Rita and P. Cortez (2014) is distributed under CC BY 4.0. The "
"bundled CSV was converted from the legacy workbook. The loader encodes subscription as 1 and non-"
"subscription as 0. See the `dataset record <https://doi.org/10.24432/C5K306>`_ and `license "
"<https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/>`_. The loan panel is synthetic and has no source "
"to attribute."
msgstr ""
"Bank Marketing 由 S. Moro、P. Rita 和 P. Cortez 于 2014 年发布，按 CC BY 4.0 授权。随包 CSV "
"由旧版工作簿转换而来。加载时将认购存款编码为 1，未认购编码为 0。详见 `数据集说明 <https://doi.org/10.24432/C5K306>`_ 和 `许可证 "
"<https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/>`_。贷款面板是合成数据，没有需要注明的来源。"

msgid ""
"kivi covers the steps of credit risk modeling: binning, variable selection, scorecard scaling, "
"model evaluation, calibration, deployment and monitoring, and the vintage and roll-rate analysis "
"of the loans a model approves. Use the same bin edges in development and monitoring so that "
"counts remain comparable."
msgstr ""
"kivi 覆盖信用风险建模的各个环节：分箱、变量筛选、评分卡刻度、模型评估、校准、部署和监控，以及对模型批准的贷款做 vintage "
"与滚动率分析。在开发和监测阶段复用同一套分箱边界，可以直接比较各组计数。"

msgid ""
"kivi keeps fitting and measuring apart. ``bin_edges`` fits edges on a reference sample, "
"``pandas.cut`` assigns every sample to those bins, and ``woe_table`` and ``psi_table`` summarize "
"the resulting groups. The metric functions accept any grouping, so category labels can be passed "
"directly."
msgstr ""
"kivi 将拟合与计算分开。``bin_edges`` 在基准样本上拟合边界，``pandas.cut`` 把每个样本划入这些箱，``woe_table`` 和 ``psi_table`` "
"再汇总得到的分组。指标函数接受任意分组，因此类别标签可以直接传入。"

msgid "Risk modeling workflow"
msgstr "风控建模流程"

msgid ""
"An end-to-end example: screen variables by IV, bin the shortlist, encode it with WOE, save the "
"binning, fit and scale a scorecard, evaluate and calibrate it, and report stability."
msgstr "端到端示例：按 IV 筛选变量，对入选变量分箱，用 WOE 编码，保存分箱，拟合评分卡并刻度为分值，评估和校准模型，并输出稳定性报告。"

msgid ""
"Quantile, uniform and custom edges, special values, merging fine bins, supervised binning and "
"missing values."
msgstr "等频、等距与自定义边界，特殊值，合并细分箱，有监督分箱以及缺失值。"

msgid ""
"Definitions, the smoothing rule for empty cells, how to read the result and how to encode new "
"data."
msgstr "定义、空单元格的平滑规则、结果的解读方法以及如何对新数据编码。"

msgid ""
"Compare the distribution of two samples, including categories seen in only one of them, and "
"measure each variable's effect on the score with CSI."
msgstr "比较两个样本的分布，包括只在其中一个样本出现的类别，并用 CSI 衡量每个变量对分数的影响。"

msgid ""
"Bin a whole data frame at once and save the edges and WOE tables as versioned JSON for production"
" scoring."
msgstr "一次对整个数据框分箱，并把边界和 WOE 表保存为带版本号的 JSON，供生产环境打分。"

msgid ""
"Correlation filtering, variance inflation factors, logistic regression and stepwise selection "
"with positive coefficients."
msgstr "相关性过滤、方差膨胀因子、逻辑回归，以及保证系数为正的逐步回归。"

msgid "PDO scaling, points per group, scores for new data and reason codes."
msgstr "PDO 刻度、每组分值、为新数据打分以及原因码。"

msgid "AUC, Gini, KS and gains tables, with the score oriented so that higher means riskier."
msgstr "AUC、Gini、KS 和增益表，分数方向约定为越高风险越大。"

msgid ""
"Prior correction, master scales, statistical tests of each grade's PD, and Platt and isotonic "
"recalibration."
msgstr "先验校正、主标尺、对每个评级 PD 的统计检验，以及 Platt 与保序回归重新校准。"

msgid ""
"Cumulative bad rates by cohort and month on book, roll rates and transition matrices between "
"delinquency buckets."
msgstr "按批次和账龄统计的累计坏账率，以及逾期档位之间的滚动率和迁移矩阵。"

msgid ""
"The bundled bank marketing data, its target and its license, and a synthetic loan panel for "
"portfolio analysis."
msgstr "随包的银行营销数据、其目标标签与许可证，以及用于资产组合分析的合成贷款面板数据。"

msgid ""
"``kivi.metrics`` measures how well a score separates events from non-events. ``roc_auc``, "
"``gini`` and ``ks`` summarize the ranking in one number, ``gains_table`` breaks it down by score "
"band, and ``brier_score`` checks predicted probabilities against the outcomes."
msgstr ""
"``kivi.metrics`` 衡量评分区分事件与非事件的能力。``roc_auc``、``gini`` 和 ``ks`` 用一个数概括排序效果，``gains_table`` "
"按评分段展开排序效果，``brier_score`` 将预测概率与实际结果对照。"

msgid "Score direction"
msgstr "评分方向"

msgid ""
"Every function expects a score that is higher for a higher event probability, such as a predicted"
" probability of default (PD). Scorecard points run the other way, because more points mean a "
"lower risk, so negate them before passing them in: ``roc_auc(-points, target)``."
msgstr "所有函数都要求事件概率越高、评分越高，例如预测的违约概率（PD）。评分卡分数的方向相反，分数越高表示风险越低，因此须先取负再传入：``roc_auc(-points, target)``。"

msgid ""
"Every function takes the score first and the target second, as ``woe_table(groups, target)`` "
"takes the groups first. scikit-learn's metrics take the target first, so check the order when "
"porting code from them."
msgstr ""
"所有函数都是评分在前、目标在后，就像 ``woe_table(groups, target)`` 把分组放在前面。scikit-learn "
"的指标函数把目标放在前面，从那里移植代码时请检查参数顺序。"

msgid ""
"As in ``woe_table``, the target is 1 for an event and 0 for a non-event. Two Series must share "
"the same index; arrays and lists are matched by position. Scores must be finite, so decide how "
"missing values are scored before evaluating the model."
msgstr "与 ``woe_table`` 相同，目标为 1 表示事件，为 0 表示非事件。两个 Series 的索引必须相同；数组和列表按位置对应。评分必须是有限值，因此评估模型之前要先确定缺失值如何评分。"

msgid "Definitions"
msgstr "定义"

msgid ""
"For :math:`n_1` events and :math:`n_0` non-events, let :math:`R_1` be the sum of the ranks of the"
" events among all scores, where tied scores share their average rank. The area under the ROC "
"curve and the Gini coefficient are"
msgstr "设有 :math:`n_1` 个事件和 :math:`n_0` 个非事件，:math:`R_1` 为事件在全部评分中的秩之和，相同评分取平均秩。ROC 曲线下面积和 Gini 系数为"

#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"\\mathrm{AUC} = \\frac{R_1 - n_1 (n_1 + 1) / 2}{n_1 n_0}, \\qquad\n"
"\\mathrm{Gini} = 2\\,\\mathrm{AUC} - 1."
msgstr ""
"\\mathrm{AUC} = \\frac{R_1 - n_1 (n_1 + 1) / 2}{n_1 n_0}, \\qquad\n"
"\\mathrm{Gini} = 2\\,\\mathrm{AUC} - 1."

msgid ""
"The AUC is the probability that a randomly chosen event scores higher than a randomly chosen non-"
"event, with ties counted as one half. A score unrelated to the target gives an AUC of about 0.5 "
"and a Gini of about 0."
msgstr "AUC 是随机抽取的一个事件比随机抽取的一个非事件评分更高的概率，评分相同时计为二分之一。与目标无关的评分，AUC 约为 0.5，Gini 约为 0。"

msgid ""
"Let :math:`F_1` and :math:`F_0` be the empirical distribution functions of the scores of events "
"and of non-events. The Kolmogorov-Smirnov statistic is their largest gap:"
msgstr "设 :math:`F_1` 和 :math:`F_0` 分别为事件评分和非事件评分的经验分布函数。Kolmogorov-Smirnov 统计量是二者的最大差距："

#, python-brace-format
msgid "\\mathrm{KS} = \\max_t \\, \\lvert F_1(t) - F_0(t) \\rvert."
msgstr "\\mathrm{KS} = \\max_t \\, \\lvert F_1(t) - F_0(t) \\rvert."

msgid ""
"The gap is taken in absolute value, as in the two-sample test. KS therefore says nothing about "
"the direction of the score, and its largest gap can come from a range of scores where the ranking"
" is reversed. Read it together with the Gini."
msgstr "差距取绝对值，与双样本检验相同。因此 KS 不反映评分的方向，其最大差距也可能来自排序方向相反的评分区间。应与 Gini 一起解读。"

msgid "A worked example"
msgstr "计算示例"

msgid ""
"Three of these six customers are events. Of the nine pairs of an event and a non-event, six are "
"ordered correctly, two are not, and one is tied at 0.4, so the AUC is :math:`(6 + 0.5) / 9`:"
msgstr "下面六位客户中有三位是事件。在九对“事件—非事件”组合中，六对排序正确，两对错误，一对在 0.4 处并列，因此 AUC 为 :math:`(6 + 0.5) / 9`："

msgid ""
"At a cut-off of 0.4, two thirds of the non-events but only one third of the events score at or "
"below it. No cut-off separates the two classes further, so the KS is one third:"
msgstr "以 0.4 为切分点，三分之二的非事件评分不高于它，而事件只有三分之一。没有哪个切分点能把两类分得更开，因此 KS 为三分之一："

msgid "Evaluating a WOE score"
msgstr "评估 WOE 评分"

msgid ""
"The bank data give a more realistic example. The score below adds up the WOE values of four "
"variables, fitted on the development sample. A higher WOE means a higher event rate, so the sum "
"already runs in the direction the metrics expect. A scorecard would weight the variables with a "
"logistic regression; the metrics treat any score in the same way."
msgstr ""
"银行数据提供了一个更贴近实际的例子。下面的评分把四个变量的 WOE 值相加，这些 WOE 在开发样本上拟合。WOE "
"越高表示事件率越高，因此这个和的方向已经符合指标的要求。评分卡会用逻辑回归为各变量加权；对任何评分，这些指标的处理方式都一样。"

msgid ""
"Measure the score on both samples. The validation rows played no part in fitting the WOE values, "
"so they show how the score holds up on new customers:"
msgstr "在两个样本上分别衡量评分。验证样本没有参与 WOE 的拟合，因此能反映评分在新客户上的表现："

msgid ""
"A clear drop from development to validation would point to overfitting. Here the validation "
"values are even slightly higher, which is within the sampling noise of 173 validation events."
msgstr "如果指标从开发样本到验证样本明显下降，可能意味着过拟合。这里验证样本的数值甚至略高，仍在 173 个验证事件的抽样误差范围之内。"

msgid ""
"Points that fall as the risk rises rank the customers in the opposite order. Passed as they are, "
"they give an AUC below 0.5 and a negative Gini; negated, they give the values above. KS is the "
"same in both directions, so it cannot reveal a reversed score:"
msgstr "风险越高分数越低的评分卡分数，会把客户按相反的顺序排列。直接传入时，AUC 低于 0.5，Gini 为负；取负后则得到上面的数值。KS 在两个方向上相同，因此无法发现评分方向反了："

msgid ""
"No threshold makes a Gini or a KS good in general: the values that can be reached depend on the "
"portfolio, the target definition and the data available. Compare a new score with the one it "
"replaces on the same validation sample."
msgstr "Gini 或 KS 没有通用的合格线：能达到的水平取决于资产组合、目标定义和可用的数据。应在同一个验证样本上，把新评分与它要替换的评分进行比较。"

msgid "Gains table"
msgstr "增益表"

msgid ""
"``gains_table`` sorts the sample into score bands, from the highest scores to the lowest. Each "
"row shows the event rate of its band and the share of all events found by reviewing that band and"
" every band above it. The default ``bins=10`` cuts the sample at the edges of ``bin_edges(score, "
"bins=10)``, and tied scores always share a band."
msgstr ""
"``gains_table`` 把样本按评分分段，从最高评分到最低评分排列。每行给出该段的事件率，以及审查该段及其以上各段时找到的事件占全部事件的比例。默认的 ``bins=10`` 在 "
"``bin_edges(score, bins=10)`` 的边界处切分样本，相同评分总在同一段。"

msgid ""
"In monitoring, fix the bands on the development sample so that every later sample is cut at the "
"same scores. Fit the edges with ``bin_edges`` and round them to readable cut-offs:"
msgstr "在监控中，评分段应在开发样本上固定，使之后的每个样本都在相同的评分处切分。用 ``bin_edges`` 拟合边界，再取整为易读的切分点："

msgid ""
"Event rate and lift of each score band, and the cumulative share of events against the cumulative"
" share of customers"
msgstr "各分数段的事件率与提升度，以及累计事件占比对累计客户占比的曲线"

msgid ""
"Left: the event rate falls from the top score band to the bottom one; the dashed line is the "
"event rate of the whole sample. Right: the gains curve rises well above the diagonal of a random "
"ordering."
msgstr "左：事件率从最高分数段到最低分数段逐级下降；虚线是整个样本的事件率。右：增益曲线明显高于随机排序的对角线。"

#, python-format
msgid ""
"The top band holds 17% of the validation customers (264 of 1,521) but 42% of the events, so its "
"event rate is 2.4 times that of the whole sample. The table checks the gap between the two "
"classes only at the four interior cut-offs, so its largest ``ks`` stays below the KS over all "
"scores:"
msgstr ""
"最高的评分段只占验证样本客户的 17%（1,521 人中的 264 人），却包含 42% 的事件，因此其事件率是整个样本的 2.4 倍。该表只在四个内部切分点上检查两类之间的差距，因此其 "
"``ks`` 的最大值低于在全部评分上计算的 KS："

msgid ""
"Every band is reported, including a band that no customer falls into, so two samples cut on the "
"same edges give tables with the same rows. Their ``total`` columns then give the PSI of the score"
" bands, here far below 0.1, the usual upper bound of a small shift (see :doc:`psi`):"
msgstr ""
"结果列出每个评分段，包括没有客户落入的评分段，因此用相同边界切分的两个样本得到的表行相同。由二者的 ``total`` 列即可得到评分段的 PSI，这里远低于 "
"0.1，即通常视为小幅变化的上限（见 :doc:`psi`）："

msgid "Reading the result"
msgstr "解读结果"

msgid "``non_event``, ``event``, ``total``"
msgstr "``non_event``, ``event``, ``total``"

msgid "Non-events, events and all observations in the band, as in ``woe_table``."
msgstr "该段的非事件数、事件数和总观测数，与 ``woe_table`` 相同。"

msgid "``event_rate``"
msgstr "``event_rate``"

msgid "``event`` divided by ``total``; NaN for an empty band."
msgstr "``event`` 除以 ``total``；空评分段为 NaN。"

msgid "``lift``"
msgstr "``lift``"

msgid "The event rate of the band divided by the event rate of the whole sample."
msgstr "该段的事件率除以整个样本的事件率。"

msgid "``cum_non_event_share``, ``cum_event_share``"
msgstr "``cum_non_event_share``, ``cum_event_share``"

msgid "Shares of all non-events and of all events in this band and the bands above it."
msgstr "该段及其以上各段分别占全部非事件和全部事件的比例。"

msgid "``cum_total_share``"
msgstr "``cum_total_share``"

msgid ""
"Share of all observations in this band and the bands above it. Plotting ``cum_event_share`` "
"against ``cum_total_share`` gives the gains chart."
msgstr "该段及其以上各段占全部观测的比例。以 ``cum_total_share`` 为横轴、``cum_event_share`` 为纵轴作图，即为增益图。"

msgid "``ks``"
msgstr "``ks``"

msgid ""
"The absolute gap between ``cum_event_share`` and ``cum_non_event_share`` at the lower edge of the"
" band. Like ``ks``, it can come from a band where the score runs the wrong way, with "
"``cum_non_event_share`` above ``cum_event_share``."
msgstr ""
"在该段下边界处，``cum_event_share`` 与 ``cum_non_event_share`` 之差的绝对值。与 ``ks`` 一样，它可能来自评分方向相反的评分段，即 "
"``cum_non_event_share`` 高于 ``cum_event_share``。"

msgid "``cum_lift``"
msgstr "``cum_lift``"

msgid ""
"``cum_event_share`` divided by ``cum_total_share``: the lift of reviewing this band and every "
"band above it."
msgstr "``cum_event_share`` 除以 ``cum_total_share``，即审查该段及其以上各段时的提升度。"

msgid "Brier score"
msgstr "Brier 分数"

msgid ""
"The ranking measures ignore the probability scale: any increasing transformation of the score "
"gives the same AUC, Gini and KS. When a model predicts probabilities, for example a PD used for "
"pricing or provisions, also compare them with the observed outcomes. ``brier_score`` is the mean "
"squared difference between the probability :math:`p_i` and the outcome :math:`y_i`, so a lower "
"value is better:"
msgstr ""
"排序度量与概率的尺度无关：对评分做任何递增变换，AUC、Gini 和 KS 都不变。如果模型预测的是概率，例如用于定价或拨备的 PD，还要把概率与观测结果对照。``brier_score`` "
"是概率 :math:`p_i` 与结果 :math:`y_i` 之差的平方的均值，因此越低越好："

#, python-brace-format
msgid "\\mathrm{BS} = \\frac{1}{n} \\sum_{i=1}^{n} (p_i - y_i)^2."
msgstr "\\mathrm{BS} = \\frac{1}{n} \\sum_{i=1}^{n} (p_i - y_i)^2."

msgid ""
"The example below predicts the probability of each validation customer by the development event "
"rate of the customer's ``poutcome`` group, and compares it with predicting the development event "
"rate for everyone:"
msgstr "下面的例子用客户所在 ``poutcome`` 组在开发样本中的事件率预测每位验证客户的概率，并与对所有人都预测开发样本事件率的做法进行比较："

#, python-format
msgid ""
"The group rates lower the Brier score by about 10% compared with the constant forecast. Unlike "
"the ranking measures, the Brier score needs no events in the sample, so it can also be computed "
"for a period without any."
msgstr "与常数预测相比，分组事件率使 Brier 分数降低了约 10%。与排序度量不同，Brier 分数不要求样本中有事件，因此在没有事件的时期也能计算。"

msgid ""
"Validation samples often keep every event but only some of the non-events. Every function of "
":mod:`kivi.metrics` takes ``weights``, one non-negative weight per observation matched like the "
"target, and then counts sums of weights instead of observations. Integer weights give the same "
"result as repeating rows, for ``gains_table`` on fixed edges: with an integer ``bins``, the "
"weighted quantiles of ``bin_edges`` use the inverted CDF and can give other edges than the "
"repeated rows. To weight a sample back to the population, give each observation the inverse of "
"its sampling rate. Below, every event of the validation sample is kept but only every second non-"
"event:"
msgstr ""
"验证样本常常保留全部事件、只保留部分非事件。 :mod:`kivi.metrics` 的每个函数都接受 ``weights`` "
"，即每个观测一个非负权重，对应方式与目标相同；此时统计的是权重之和而不是观测个数。整数权重与重复相应行的结果相同，对 ``gains_table`` 而言须使用固定边界：若 ``bins`` "
"为整数， ``bin_edges`` "
"的加权分位数采用逆累积分布，得到的边界可能与重复行不同。要把样本加权还原到总体，给每个观测赋予其抽样比例的倒数。下面保留验证样本中的全部事件，但非事件每两个只保留一个："

msgid ""
"Without weights the sample has twice as many events per non-event as the population, and every "
"band's event rate is inflated. The weights restore rates close to those of all customers. The "
"ranking measures do not change, because a weight that is the same for every observation of a "
"class cancels out of the AUC, the Gini and the KS:"
msgstr ""
"不加权时，样本中每个非事件对应的事件数是总体的两倍，每个评分段的事件率都被抬高。加权后，事件率恢复到与全部客户接近的水平。排序指标不变，因为对同一类的每个观测都相同的权重会在 AUC、Gini "
"和 KS 中相互抵消："

msgid ""
"Weights that differ within a class, such as the inverse sampling rates of a stratified sample, do"
" change them."
msgstr "同一类内部各不相同的权重（例如分层样本的抽样比例倒数）则会改变这些指标。"

msgid ""
"``psi_table`` compares the distribution of a variable in two samples, typically the development "
"sample and a later monitoring sample. Group both samples with the same edges or labels before "
"calling it. ``csi_table`` measures how much such a change moves a scorecard's score; see :ref"
":`characteristic-stability`."
msgstr ""
"``psi_table`` 比较一个变量在两个样本中的分布，通常是开发样本和之后的监测样本。调用前，请用同一组边界或标签对两个样本分组。 ``csi_table`` "
"衡量这种变化使评分卡分数移动了多少，参见 :ref:`characteristic-stability` 。"

msgid "Definition"
msgstr "定义"

msgid ""
"Each contribution is zero or positive. PSI describes distribution change; it does not use the "
"outcome label."
msgstr "每一项贡献都大于或等于零。PSI 描述的是分布变化，不使用目标标签。"

msgid "Missing values and new categories"
msgstr "缺失值与新类别"

msgid ""
"Missing values form their own group, and categories appearing in only one sample are retained. "
"Their empty cells are smoothed exactly as in :doc:`woe_iv`, so every contribution stays finite."
msgstr "缺失值单独成组，只在一个样本中出现的类别也会保留。它们的空单元格按 :doc:`woe_iv` 中的方式平滑，因此每一项贡献都是有限值。"

msgid ""
"When only the counts per group are available, for example from a monitoring report, ``psi`` gives"
" the total from the counts of each sample in the same group order:"
msgstr "如果只有每组的计数（例如来自监控报表），可以用 ``psi`` 按相同的分组顺序传入两个样本的计数，得到总的 PSI："

msgid ""
"For weighted samples, pass ``reference_weights`` and ``current_weights`` to ``psi_table``; the "
"counts are then sums of weights."
msgstr "对于加权样本，请把 ``reference_weights`` 和 ``current_weights`` 传给 ``psi_table`` ；此时计数为权重之和。"

msgid "Stable and shifted samples"
msgstr "稳定与偏移的样本"

msgid ""
"Two samples from the same population give a PSI close to zero. When the population changes, the "
"bins that moved stand out. Below, the current sample is replaced by single customers only, who "
"are much younger than the reference."
msgstr "来自同一客群的两个样本，PSI 接近于零。客群发生变化时，发生移动的箱会凸显出来。下面把当前样本换成只包含单身客户的样本，他们比基准样本年轻得多。"

msgid "Reference and current age distributions for a random split and for single customers"
msgstr "随机切分样本与单身客户样本的基准、当前年龄分布"

msgid ""
"Left: the remaining customers look like the reference sample. Right: single customers crowd into "
"the youngest bin, and the youngest and oldest bins contribute most of the PSI."
msgstr "左图：其余客户与基准样本基本一致。右图：单身客户集中在最年轻的箱，最年轻和最年长的两个箱贡献了大部分 PSI。"

msgid "``reference``, ``current``"
msgstr "``reference``, ``current``"

msgid "Observed counts in each group."
msgstr "每组的实际观测数。"

msgid "``reference_share``, ``current_share``"
msgstr "``reference_share``, ``current_share``"

msgid ":math:`q_i` and :math:`p_i` after smoothing; each column sums to 1."
msgstr "平滑后的 :math:`q_i` 和 :math:`p_i`；每列之和为 1。"

msgid "``psi``"
msgstr "``psi``"

msgid "The group's contribution. Sum the column to obtain total drift."
msgstr "该组的贡献。对该列求和得到整体漂移。"

msgid ""
"A common convention reads a PSI below 0.1 as a small shift, 0.1 to 0.25 as a moderate shift and "
"above 0.25 as a large shift. The thresholds depend on the number of bins and on the smoothing "
"rule, so recheck them when moving analyses from 0.2.x."
msgstr "一种常见的经验口径是：PSI 低于 0.1 视为变化较小，0.1 到 0.25 为中等变化，高于 0.25 为显著变化。这些阈值取决于箱数和平滑规则，从 0.2.x 迁移分析时请重新核对。"

msgid "Monitoring over time"
msgstr "按期监控"

msgid ""
"In production, PSI is computed for every period against the development sample and compared with "
"the conventions above. The bank data record the month of the last contact but not the year, so "
"the months below mix several years; read them as an example of a monitoring report."
msgstr "在生产环境中，每一期都要相对开发样本计算 PSI，并按上面的经验口径判断。银行数据只记录了最后一次联系的月份而没有年份，因此下面的月份混合了多个年份，请把它看作一份监控报告的示例。"

msgid ""
"PSI of age for each contact month, with the 0.1 and 0.25 thresholds and the sample size of each "
"month"
msgstr "每个联系月份 age 的 PSI，含 0.1 与 0.25 阈值及各月样本量"

msgid ""
"PSI of age for each contact month against the reference sample, with the number of customers "
"under each month."
msgstr "每个联系月份的 age 相对基准样本的 PSI，各月下方标注了客户数。"

msgid ""
"The months that cross the thresholds are also the smallest. With 20 customers, the December value"
" mostly reflects sampling noise. Set a minimum sample size before a high PSI raises an alert."
msgstr "越过阈值的月份恰好也是样本最少的月份。12 月只有 20 位客户，其 PSI 主要反映抽样噪声。在用高 PSI 触发预警之前，应先设定最小样本量。"

msgid "Characteristic stability index"
msgstr "特征稳定性指标"

msgid ""
"PSI shows that a distribution has moved, but not what the move does to the score. The "
"characteristic stability index (CSI) weights the change of each group's share with the scorecard "
"points :math:`s_i` of the group:"
msgstr "PSI 能说明分布发生了移动，却不能说明这种移动对分数有什么影响。特征稳定性指标（CSI）以每组的评分卡分值 :math:`s_i` 为权重，衡量各组占比的变化："

#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"\\mathrm{CSI}_i = (p_i - q_i)\\, s_i, \\qquad\n"
"\\mathrm{CSI} = \\sum_i \\mathrm{CSI}_i = \\sum_i p_i s_i - \\sum_i q_i s_i."
msgstr ""
"\\mathrm{CSI}_i = (p_i - q_i)\\, s_i, \\qquad\n"
"\\mathrm{CSI} = \\sum_i \\mathrm{CSI}_i = \\sum_i p_i s_i - \\sum_i q_i s_i."

msgid ""
"The CSI is the change of the variable's average points from the reference to the current sample: "
"a negative CSI means that the variable now gives fewer points on average. Over all the variables "
"of a scorecard, the CSI values add up to the change of the average score. Since the shares of "
"each sample sum to 1, adding the same number to the points of every group leaves the CSI "
"unchanged, so only the differences between the groups matter."
msgstr ""
"CSI 是该变量平均分值从基准样本到当前样本的变化：CSI 为负，说明该变量现在平均给出的分值更少。对评分卡的所有变量，CSI 之和就是平均分数的变化。由于每个样本的占比之和都为 "
"1，给每组的分值加上同一个数不会改变 CSI，因此起作用的只是各组之间的差别。"

msgid ""
"Some texts call the PSI of a single variable its CSI. kivi follows the score-weighted definition "
"of the characteristic analysis report; for the PSI of a variable, use ``psi_table`` on its groups"
" as above."
msgstr "有些文献把单个变量的 PSI 称为它的 CSI。kivi 采用特征分析报告中按分值加权的定义；要计算某个变量的 PSI，请像上文那样对其分组调用 ``psi_table`` 。"

msgid ""
"The example uses the scorecard of :doc:`scorecard`. Fit the WOE of four variables on the "
"development sample and turn the model into points:"
msgstr "示例使用 :doc:`scorecard` 中的评分卡。在开发样本上拟合四个变量的 WOE，并把模型转换为分值："

msgid ""
"``csi_table`` takes the groups of both samples and the points of the variable's groups, here the "
"rows of the points table for age:"
msgstr "``csi_table`` 接受两个样本的分组以及该变量各分组的分值，这里取分值表中 age 的各行："

msgid ""
"The shares are not smoothed, unlike those of ``psi_table``. A contribution has no logarithm, so "
"an empty group contributes a finite amount as it is, and a smoothed share would credit an empty "
"group with customers it does not have: the sum would no longer be the change of the average "
"points."
msgstr "与 ``psi_table`` 不同，这里的占比不做平滑。贡献中没有对数，因此空组无需平滑也只有有限的贡献；而平滑后的占比会让空组拥有它并没有的客户，求和结果也就不再是平均分值的变化。"

msgid ""
"A characteristic analysis report lists both indices for every variable of the scorecard. The CSI "
"column adds up to the change of the average score, here less than a fifth of a point:"
msgstr "特征分析报告列出评分卡每个变量的这两个指标。CSI 列之和就是平均分数的变化，这里不到五分之一分："

msgid ""
"The two indices answer different questions. Single customers, from the shifted sample above, have"
" a very different age distribution, but the age bands they crowd into have about the same points "
"as the others, so age lowers their average score by less than half a point:"
msgstr "这两个指标回答的是不同的问题。上文偏移样本中的单身客户，年龄分布差别很大，但这些客户集中的年龄段与其他年龄段的分值相差无几，因此年龄只让其平均分数降低不到半分："

msgid ""
"A group without points, such as a category that the development sample did not have, raises an "
"error unless ``unseen_points`` gives the points that its customers receive. These are points, not"
" a WOE: if ``woe_transform`` encoded the category with ``unseen=0.0``, pass the points of a WOE "
"of 0, ``woe_to_points`` of a one-row frame of zeros, which are the same for every variable. For "
"weighted samples, pass ``reference_weights`` and ``current_weights`` as for ``psi_table``."
msgstr ""
"没有分值的分组（例如开发样本中没有的类别）会引发错误，除非用 ``unseen_points`` 给出其客户得到的分值。这里要传入的是分值而不是 WOE：如果 ``woe_transform``"
" 用 ``unseen=0.0`` 编码了该类别，就传入 WOE 为 0 时的分值，即对一行全零调用 ``woe_to_points`` 的结果，每个变量都相同。对加权样本，像 "
"``psi_table`` 一样传入 ``reference_weights`` 和 ``current_weights`` 。"

msgid ""
"This example follows the steps of a scorecard project with kivi: screen the candidate variables, "
"bin the shortlist, encode it with WOE and save the binning for production, select the variables "
"and fit the model, scale it to a scorecard, evaluate and calibrate it, and prepare the stability "
"report used in monitoring. The bundled data record a marketing response rather than a default, "
"but the steps are the same for a credit default flag: use the bad flag as ``target``."
msgstr ""
"本示例用 kivi 走一遍评分卡项目的各个步骤：筛选候选变量，对入选变量分箱，用 WOE "
"编码并保存分箱供生产环境使用，筛选变量并拟合模型，刻度为评分卡，评估并校准模型，并准备监控所需的稳定性报告。随包数据记录的是营销响应而非违约，但对信用违约标记来说步骤完全相同：把坏样本标记作为 "
"``target`` 即可。"

msgid "Screen variables by IV"
msgstr "按 IV 筛选变量"

msgid ""
"Start with a quick, uniform binning of every candidate: five quantile bins for numeric variables "
"and the raw labels for categorical ones. The IV of each variable gives a first ranking. "
"``bin_edges`` warns when tied values leave fewer bins than requested; the loop records those "
"variables instead of printing the warnings."
msgstr ""
"先对每个候选变量做一次快速、统一的分箱：数值变量用 5 个等频箱，类别变量直接使用原始标签。各变量的 IV 给出初步排序。重复取值使箱数少于要求时， ``bin_edges`` "
"会发出警告；这里的循环把这些变量记录下来，而不是打印警告。"

msgid ""
"Information value of every variable in the bank data, sorted, with the 0.02, 0.1 and 0.3 reading "
"bands"
msgstr "银行数据中各变量的信息值排序，含 0.02、0.1 和 0.3 的解读区间"

msgid ""
"IV of every candidate variable with quick binning. The dashed lines mark the 0.02, 0.1 and 0.3 "
"bands; ``duration`` is cut off at the right edge of the chart."
msgstr "快速分箱下各候选变量的 IV。虚线标出 0.02、0.1 和 0.3 三个区间；``duration`` 的柱子在图的右边缘被截断。"

msgid "Read the ranking critically before building the shortlist:"
msgstr "在确定入选名单之前，请审慎地解读这个排序："

msgid ""
"``duration`` is the length of the last call. It is only known after the call, when the outcome is"
" largely decided, so its IV of 1.59 is a leak rather than a signal. The dataset's documentation "
"recommends leaving it out of a realistic model. In credit risk, look for the same pattern in "
"fields filled in after the decision, such as collection status."
msgstr ""
"``duration`` 是最后一次通话的时长。它只有在通话结束后才知道，而那时结果基本已经确定，因此它 1.59 的 IV "
"是信息泄漏而非有效信号。数据集的说明建议在构建实际可用的模型时排除它。在信用风险中，也要警惕在决策之后才填写的字段，例如催收状态。"

msgid ""
"``month`` describes when the campaign ran rather than who the customer is, so it is left out as "
"well."
msgstr "``month`` 描述的是营销活动开展的时间，而不是客户本身，因此同样排除。"

msgid ""
"``pdays`` and ``previous`` show an IV of zero only because their tied values collapse into one "
"quantile bin. Custom edges or the ``special`` argument recover ``pdays``; see :ref:`custom-edges`"
" and :ref:`special-values`."
msgstr ""
"``pdays`` 和 ``previous`` 的 IV 为零，只是因为大量重复值使它们被压缩进一个等频箱。自定义边界或 ``special`` 参数都可以挽回 ``pdays`` ，见 "
":ref:`custom-edges` 和 :ref:`special-values` 。"

msgid "Bin the shortlist"
msgstr "对入选变量分箱"

msgid ""
"Each variable on the shortlist gets edges that can be explained: merged balance bins with a "
"monotonic WOE, a bin of its own for the ``pdays == -1`` code, policy age bands, and the raw "
"labels of the categorical variables. Keep the binning in one place so that development and "
"monitoring data are grouped identically."
msgstr ""
"每个入选变量都使用可以解释的边界：余额采用合并后 WOE 单调的分箱，``pdays == -1`` "
"编码单独成箱，年龄采用政策分段，类别变量使用原始标签。把分箱逻辑集中在一处，确保开发数据和监控数据的分组完全一致。"

msgid ""
"``tables`` holds one ``woe_table`` result per variable. Review each one as a WOE chart (see "
":doc:`woe_iv`) before moving on. ``pdays`` and ``poutcome`` both describe the previous campaign, "
"so check how strongly they are correlated before keeping both."
msgstr ""
"``tables`` 为每个变量保存一个 ``woe_table`` 结果。继续之前，请逐一以 WOE 图的形式复核（见 :doc:`woe_iv`）。``pdays`` 和 "
"``poutcome`` 都描述上一轮营销，同时保留之前请先检查二者的相关性。"

msgid "Encode with WOE"
msgstr "WOE 编码"

msgid ""
"A logistic regression on WOE values is the classic scorecard model. Replace each group with the "
"WOE from the development tables using ``woe_transform``:"
msgstr "基于 WOE 值的逻辑回归是经典的评分卡模型。用 ``woe_transform`` 把每个分组替换为开发样本表中对应的 WOE："

msgid ""
"``woe_transform`` raises an error for a group that never appeared in development, such as a new "
"category. Agree on a policy before scoring new data, for example ``unseen=0.0`` for a neutral "
"WOE."
msgstr "对开发样本中从未出现的分组（例如新类别）， ``woe_transform`` 会引发错误。对新数据评分之前，请先约定处理方式，例如用 ``unseen=0.0`` 取中性的 WOE。"

msgid "Save the binning"
msgstr "保存分箱"

msgid ""
"Production systems must group and encode new applications exactly as the development sample was. "
"``fit_spec`` fits the edges and the WOE table of every column at once, and the resulting "
"``BinningSpec`` saves them as versioned JSON; see :doc:`spec`. Passing the edges of the shortlist"
" as ``bins`` reproduces the encoding above:"
msgstr ""
"生产系统对新申请的分组和编码必须与开发样本完全一致。 ``fit_spec`` 一次拟合每列的边界和 WOE 表，得到的 ``BinningSpec`` 把它们保存为带版本号的 JSON；参见 "
":doc:`spec` 。把入选变量的边界作为 ``bins`` 传入，即可复现上面的编码："

msgid ""
"Store the JSON with the model. A scoring service that loads it with ``BinningSpec.from_json`` "
"encodes new data with ``restored.woe_transform(frame)``, without the code of the development "
"project."
msgstr ""
"把 JSON 与模型一起保存。打分服务用 ``BinningSpec.from_json`` 加载后，用 ``restored.woe_transform(frame)`` "
"对新数据编码，无需开发项目的代码。"

msgid "Select variables and fit the model"
msgstr "筛选变量并拟合模型"

msgid ""
"Strongly correlated variables carry the same information and make the coefficients unstable. "
"``correlation_filter`` keeps the variable with the higher IV from each pair correlated above 0.7,"
" and ``stepwise`` then selects variables by the p-values of a logistic regression. With WOE "
"inputs every coefficient should be positive, and ``stepwise`` rejects a variable that would make "
"one negative; see :doc:`selection`."
msgstr ""
"高度相关的变量携带相同的信息，还会让系数不稳定。 ``correlation_filter`` 在每对相关系数超过 0.7 的变量中保留 IV 较高的一个，随后 ``stepwise`` "
"按逻辑回归的 p 值筛选变量。以 WOE 作为输入时，所有系数都应为正， ``stepwise`` 会拒绝会使某个系数变为负的变量；详见 :doc:`selection` 。"

msgid ""
"No pair is correlated strongly enough to drop a variable, and ``stepwise`` leaves out ``age``. "
"The model is fitted on the development sample only."
msgstr "没有哪对变量的相关性高到需要剔除， ``stepwise`` 去掉了 ``age`` 。模型只用开发样本拟合。"

msgid "Scale to a scorecard"
msgstr "刻度为评分卡"

msgid ""
"``points_table`` turns the WOE tables and the coefficients into points for every group. Here 20 "
"points double the odds of a good outcome, and a score of 600 stands for good:bad odds of 50; see "
":doc:`scorecard`. A higher WOE means more risk and therefore fewer points:"
msgstr ""
"``points_table`` 把 WOE 表和系数转换为每组的分值。这里每增加 20 分，好坏比翻一倍；600 分对应 50 的好坏比；详见 :doc:`scorecard` 。WOE "
"越高风险越大，分值也就越低："

msgid ""
"Score the monitoring sample with the development tables: each customer's score is the sum of "
"their points."
msgstr "用开发样本的表给监控样本打分：每个客户的分数是其各项分值之和。"

msgid "Evaluate the model"
msgstr "评估模型"

msgid ""
"A higher score means lower risk, while the measures in :doc:`metrics` expect a score that rises "
"with the event probability. Pass the probability that each score stands for. The gains table uses"
" bands fitted on the development scores, so that both samples are cut alike:"
msgstr "分数越高风险越低，而 :doc:`metrics` 中的指标要求分数随事件概率升高。因此请传入每个分数对应的概率。增益表使用在开发样本分数上拟合的分段，使两个样本按同样的方式切分："

#, python-format
msgid ""
"The riskiest band, about a fifth of the monitoring sample, holds 48% of its events at about twice"
" the average event rate."
msgstr "风险最高的分段约占监控样本的五分之一，却包含了 48% 的事件，事件率约为平均水平的两倍。"

msgid "Check calibration"
msgstr "检查校准"

msgid ""
"Group the monitoring sample into rating grades by PD and compare each grade's event rate with the"
" mean PD of its customers; see :doc:`calibration`. The Jeffreys test asks whether a grade has "
"more events than its PD predicts, so a small p-value flags a grade that underestimates risk:"
msgstr ""
"按 PD 把监控样本分成若干评级，并比较每个评级的事件率与其客户的平均 PD；详见 :doc:`calibration` 。Jeffreys 检验考察某个评级的事件数是否多于其 PD "
"的预测，因此 p 值较小说明该评级低估了风险："

#, python-format
msgid ""
"No grade is rejected at the 5% level. Grade D has fewer events than predicted, which this one-"
"sided test does not flag."
msgstr "在 5% 的水平下没有评级被拒绝。评级 D 的事件数少于预测，这种单侧检验不会对此报警。"

msgid "Report stability"
msgstr "稳定性报告"

msgid ""
"Compare each variable of the monitoring sample with its development distribution. The status "
"column applies the PSI conventions from :doc:`psi`."
msgstr "把监控样本中的每个变量与其开发样本分布比较。status 列采用 :doc:`psi` 中的 PSI 经验口径。"

msgid ""
"Every variable is stable here, as expected when the monitoring rows come from the same "
"population. The ``csi`` column weights each group's change of share with its points, so it is the"
" change of the variable's average points; ``age`` is not in the scorecard and has none. Over the "
"variables of the scorecard, the CSI adds up to the change of the average score:"
msgstr ""
"这里所有变量都是稳定的，监控数据与开发数据来自同一客群时理应如此。 ``csi`` 列用各组的分值对其占比变化加权，因此等于该变量平均分值的变化； ``age`` 不在评分卡中，所以没有 "
"CSI。对评分卡的所有变量求和，CSI 等于平均分的变化："

msgid "The score itself is monitored the same way, with bands fitted on the development scores:"
msgstr "分数本身也按同样的方式监控，使用在开发样本分数上拟合的分段："

msgid ":doc:`psi` shows what a shift looks like and how to track PSI period by period."
msgstr ":doc:`psi` 展示了偏移的样子以及如何按期跟踪 PSI。"

msgid ""
"A scorecard turns a logistic regression on WOE values into points. Every applicant receives the "
"points of their group in each variable, and the points add up to a score that stands for the odds"
" of a good outcome. kivi takes the coefficients and the intercept as plain numbers, so the model "
"can come from any library."
msgstr "评分卡把基于 WOE 的逻辑回归转换为分值。每个申请人在每个变量上获得其所属分组的分值，这些分值相加得到一个代表好结果几率的分数。kivi 把系数和截距当作普通数值接收，因此模型可以来自任何库。"

msgid "Scaling"
msgstr "刻度"

#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"A score is linear in the log of the good:bad odds :math:`o = (1 - \\mathrm{PD}) / \\mathrm{PD}`. "
"Three numbers set the scale: the base score, the odds at the base score and the points to double "
"the odds (PDO):"
msgstr ""
"分数与好坏比 :math:`o = (1 - \\mathrm{PD}) / \\mathrm{PD}` "
"的对数呈线性关系。刻度由三个数决定：基准分数、基准分数对应的几率，以及几率翻倍所需增加的分数（PDO）："

msgid ""
"Every function of :mod:`kivi.scorecard` takes the three numbers as keyword arguments, so keep "
"them together in one dictionary:"
msgstr ":mod:`kivi.scorecard` 的每个函数都以关键字参数接收这三个数，因此可以把它们放在同一个字典里："

msgid ""
"On this scale, odds of 50:1, a PD of 1/51, score 600, and odds of 100:1 score 20 points more. "
"``score_to_pd`` converts in the other direction:"
msgstr "在这一刻度下，几率 50:1（即 PD 为 1/51）对应 600 分，几率 100:1 则多 20 分。 ``score_to_pd`` 进行反向转换："

msgid ""
"kivi's WOE is :math:`\\ln(p_i / q_i)`, the event share over the non-event share, with the bad "
"outcome as the event (see :doc:`woe_iv`). A higher WOE therefore means more risk, a logistic "
"regression of the bad flag on WOE values has positive coefficients, and a higher WOE gives fewer "
"points. Some textbooks define WOE the other way round; their coefficients and WOE values both "
"change sign, and the points stay the same."
msgstr ""
"kivi 的 WOE 为 :math:`\\ln(p_i / q_i)` ，即事件占比与非事件占比之比的对数，并以坏结果作为事件（参见 :doc:`woe_iv` ）。因此 WOE "
"越高表示风险越高，以坏标记为因变量、以 WOE 为自变量的逻辑回归系数为正，WOE 越高得到的分值越低。有些教材的 WOE 定义方向相反；此时系数和 WOE 值都会变号，而分值保持不变。"

msgid "Points for each group"
msgstr "每个分组的分值"

msgid ""
"The example below builds a small scorecard on the bundled bank data. The data record a marketing "
"response rather than a default, so read target 1 as the bad outcome, as in :doc:`risk_workflow`. "
"Group the development sample and fit the WOE of each variable:"
msgstr ""
"下面的示例在随包附带的银行数据上构建一张小型评分卡。这份数据记录的是营销响应而非违约，因此与 :doc:`risk_workflow` 一样，把 target 为 1 "
"视为坏结果。先对开发样本分组，并拟合每个变量的 WOE："

msgid ""
"A logistic regression of ``target`` on the four WOE columns of the development sample gives the "
"coefficients and the intercept below, rounded to three decimals. ``points_table`` turns them into"
" points:"
msgstr "在开发样本上以 ``target`` 为因变量、以四个 WOE 列为自变量做逻辑回归，得到下面的系数和截距（保留三位小数）。 ``points_table`` 把它们转换为分值："

msgid "Group :math:`i` of variable :math:`j`, one of :math:`m` variables, receives"
msgstr "共有 :math:`m` 个变量时，变量 :math:`j` 的第 :math:`i` 组得到"

msgid ""
"\\mathrm{points}_{ij} = \\frac{\\mathrm{offset} - \\mathrm{factor} \\cdot \\beta_0}{m}\n"
"- \\mathrm{factor} \\cdot \\beta_j \\, \\mathrm{WOE}_{ij}."
msgstr ""
"\\mathrm{points}_{ij} = \\frac{\\mathrm{offset} - \\mathrm{factor} \\cdot \\beta_0}{m}\n"
"- \\mathrm{factor} \\cdot \\beta_j \\, \\mathrm{WOE}_{ij}."

msgid ""
"The intercept :math:`\\beta_0` and the offset are spread evenly across the variables, so each of "
"the four variables above carries a quarter of :math:`487.12 + 28.85 \\times 2.028 = 545.64` "
"points. Within a variable, the points of two groups differ only by their WOE term. A group with a"
" WOE of zero, which has the event rate of the whole sample, receives exactly the variable's "
"share."
msgstr ""
"截距 :math:`\\beta_0` 和偏移量平均分摊到各个变量，因此上面四个变量各自承担 :math:`487.12 + 28.85 \\times 2.028 = 545.64` "
"分的四分之一。在同一变量内，两个分组的分值只在 WOE 项上有差别。WOE 为零的分组，其事件率与整个样本相同，恰好得到该变量分摊的份额。"

msgid ""
"A negative coefficient reverses a variable's direction, so that riskier groups receive more "
"points. It usually points to correlated variables; review the signs before scaling a model."
msgstr "负的系数会使变量的方向反转，让风险更高的分组得到更多分值。这通常说明变量之间存在相关性；在对模型做刻度转换之前，请检查系数的符号。"

msgid "Scoring applicants"
msgstr "为申请人评分"

msgid ""
"Encode new applicants with the development WOE tables, as described in :doc:`woe_iv`, and give "
"them the points of each variable with ``woe_to_points``. The row sums are the scores:"
msgstr "按 :doc:`woe_iv` 中的方法，用开发样本的 WOE 表对新申请人编码，再用 ``woe_to_points`` 给出每个变量的分值。每行之和即为分数："

msgid ""
"The score is the scaled log odds of the model, so it equals ``pd_to_score`` of the model's "
"probability:"
msgstr "分数就是模型对数几率经刻度转换后的结果，因此等于 ``pd_to_score`` 对模型概率给出的分数："

msgid ""
"Deployed scorecards usually round the points to whole numbers. Round the points table and the "
"applicant points in the same way, with ``table.round()`` and ``points.round()``: "
"``woe_to_points`` computes each point exactly as ``points_table`` does, so the rounded values "
"match. The rounded total can differ from the exact score by up to half a point per variable."
msgstr ""
"上线的评分卡通常把分值取整。请用 ``table.round()`` 和 ``points.round()`` 以同样的方式对分值表和申请人分值取整： ``woe_to_points`` "
"的每个分值与 ``points_table`` 的计算方式完全一致，因此取整后的结果也相同。取整后的总分与精确分数之差，每个变量最多半分。"

msgid "Reason codes"
msgstr "原因码"

msgid ""
"A declined applicant is told which variables lowered the score most. ``reason_codes`` matches the"
" points of each variable to a group of the points table, compares them with those of the "
"variable's best group and lists the variables from the largest shortfall:"
msgstr "被拒绝的申请人会被告知哪些变量让分数降低最多。 ``reason_codes`` 把每个变量的分值匹配到分值表中的某个分组，与该变量最佳分组的分值比较，并按差距从大到小列出变量："

msgid ""
"Applicant 3000 was contacted by telephone, 21.3 points below the best contact group, and has no "
"housing loan, 13.2 points below the best housing group. Applicant 3001 is in the best group of "
"every variable, so no variable lowered the score."
msgstr ""
"申请人 3000 通过固定电话联系，比 contact 的最佳分组少 21.3 分；没有住房贷款，比 housing 的最佳分组少 13.2 分。申请人 3001 "
"在每个变量上都处于最佳分组，因此没有变量拉低其分数。"

#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"The scaling does not change the order of the reasons, because every shortfall is "
":math:`\\mathrm{factor} \\cdot \\beta_j` times a difference in WOE. Points that match no group of"
" the table within ``atol``, for example points computed with another intercept, raise an error "
"instead of giving reasons against the wrong groups."
msgstr ""
"刻度不会改变原因的顺序，因为每个差距都等于 :math:`\\mathrm{factor} \\cdot \\beta_j` 乘以 WOE 之差。在 ``atol`` "
"范围内无法匹配分值表中任何分组的分值（例如用其他截距算出的分值）会引发错误，而不会对照错误的分组给出原因。"

msgid ""
"Applicants in a group without development observations, such as a new category, have no group of "
"their own in the table. Their WOE comes from ``unseen`` in ``woe_transform``, a value chosen for "
"the group rather than evidence about the applicant, so by default their points raise an error "
"too. Pass their points as ``unseen_points`` to count them as costing nothing: the variable is "
"then not a reason for those applicants. ``unseen_points`` holds points, not a WOE. Run "
"``woe_to_points`` on a one-row frame that holds the WOE given to ``unseen``; a WOE of 0 gives the"
" base points, the same for every variable. Below, the first applicant has a housing status that "
"the development sample did not have:"
msgstr ""
"开发样本中没有观测的分组（例如新类别）里的申请人，在分值表中没有自己的分组。其 WOE 来自 ``woe_transform`` 中的 ``unseen`` "
"，这是为该分组选定的取值，而不是关于申请人的证据，因此默认情况下这些分值同样会引发错误。把它们的分值作为 ``unseen_points`` "
"传入，即可视为没有造成损失：此时该变量不会成为这些申请人的原因。 ``unseen_points`` 是分值而不是 WOE：对包含 ``unseen`` 所给 WOE 的单行数据调用 "
"``woe_to_points`` 即可得到；WOE 为 0 时得到基础分值，每个变量都相同。下例中，第一个申请人的住房状况在开发样本中从未出现："

msgid ""
"The first applicant's housing points are those of a WOE of 0, so only the telephone contact is a "
"reason. The second applicant has no housing loan, the less favourable housing group, and is in "
"the best contact group, ``unknown``. Only points near ``unseen_points`` are exempt: points from "
"another model, or WOE values rounded more coarsely than ``atol`` allows, still raise an error."
msgstr ""
"第一个申请人的 housing 分值就是 WOE 为 0 时的分值，因此只有电话联系方式（telephone）是原因。第二个申请人没有住房贷款，属于较不利的住房分组，并且处于最佳的联系方式分组 "
"``unknown`` 。只有接近 ``unseen_points`` 的分值才会豁免：来自其他模型的分值，或舍入比 ``atol`` 允许的更粗的 WOE，仍会引发错误。"

msgid ""
"A model developed on a sample that over- or undersamples bad outcomes has an intercept for that "
"sample. Correct it with :func:`kivi.calibration.corrected_intercept` before building the points "
"table; see :doc:`calibration`."
msgstr ""
"如果开发样本对坏结果做了过采样或欠采样，模型的截距只适用于该样本。在构建分值表之前，请用 :func:`kivi.calibration.corrected_intercept` 校正截距；参见"
" :doc:`calibration` 。"

msgid ""
"A scorecard is a logistic regression on a short list of WOE-encoded variables. ``kivi.selection``"
" covers the usual steps from the candidates to that list: drop one variable of each strongly "
"correlated pair, check the rest for collinearity, select variables by their p-values and read the"
" fitted model. Every function takes a DataFrame with one WOE-encoded column per variable, such as"
" the output of ``woe_transform``, and the functions that fit a model also take the 0/1 target."
msgstr ""
"评分卡是基于少量 WOE 编码变量的逻辑回归。 ``kivi.selection`` 涵盖了从候选变量到入选名单的常用步骤：对每一对强相关的变量剔除其中一个，检查其余变量的共线性，按 p "
"值筛选变量，并解读拟合的模型。每个函数都接收一个每个变量一列 WOE 编码值的 DataFrame，例如 ``woe_transform`` 的输出；拟合模型的函数还需要 0/1 目标变量。"

msgid "Prepare the candidates"
msgstr "准备候选变量"

msgid ""
"Group every candidate as in :doc:`risk_workflow`: quantile bins for most numeric variables, "
"explicit edges where tied values would collapse the quantiles, and the raw labels of categorical "
"variables. Then fit one WOE table per variable on the development sample, rank the variables by "
"IV and encode those with an IV of at least 0.02."
msgstr ""
"按 :doc:`risk_workflow` "
"中的方式对每个候选变量分组：多数数值变量使用分位数分箱，重复值会使分位数重合的变量使用显式边界，类别变量直接使用原始标签。然后在开发样本上为每个变量拟合一张 WOE 表，按 IV 排序，并对 "
"IV 不低于 0.02 的变量做 WOE 编码。"

msgid "Correlated variables"
msgstr "相关变量"

msgid ""
"Variables that describe the same behavior carry the same information twice. ``poutcome``, "
"``pdays`` and ``previous`` all describe the previous campaign:"
msgstr "描述同一行为的变量会重复携带相同的信息。 ``poutcome`` 、 ``pdays`` 和 ``previous`` 都描述上一次营销活动："

msgid ""
"``correlation_filter`` visits the variables from the highest ``priority`` to the lowest and keeps"
" a variable unless its absolute correlation with a variable already kept exceeds ``threshold`` "
"(0.7 by default). Pass the IV as the priority, so that of two correlated variables the more "
"predictive one stays:"
msgstr ""
"``correlation_filter`` 按 ``priority`` 从高到低依次考察各变量，若某变量与已保留变量的相关系数绝对值超过 ``threshold`` （默认 "
"0.7）则将其剔除，否则保留。把 IV 作为优先级传入，两个相关变量中预测力更强的一个就会被保留："

msgid ""
"``previous`` is dropped for ``pdays``, which has a higher IV. ``poutcome`` and ``pdays`` stay "
"together because their correlation of 0.68 is below the threshold. Thresholds between 0.6 and 0.8"
" are common; a lower one gives a shorter list."
msgstr ""
"``previous`` 因与 IV 更高的 ``pdays`` 相关而被剔除。 ``poutcome`` 与 ``pdays`` 的相关系数为 "
"0.68，低于阈值，因此二者都被保留。常用的阈值在 0.6 到 0.8 之间；阈值越低，入选名单越短。"

msgid "Variance inflation factor"
msgstr "方差膨胀因子"

msgid ""
"A correlation compares two variables, but a variable can also be explained by several others "
"together. The variance inflation factor (VIF) regresses each variable on all the others: it is 1 "
"for a variable that the others do not explain and grows without bound as they explain it "
"completely. The square root of the VIF is the factor by which collinearity inflates the standard "
"error of the variable's coefficient."
msgstr ""
"相关系数只比较两个变量，但一个变量也可能由其他几个变量共同解释。方差膨胀因子（VIF）将每个变量对其他所有变量做回归：其他变量完全无法解释的变量 VIF 为 1；其他变量越接近完全解释它，VIF"
" 越大，且没有上限。VIF 的平方根是共线性使该变量系数的标准误放大的倍数。"

msgid ""
"A common rule of thumb flags a VIF above 5, or above 10, as harmful collinearity. Every value "
"here is well below that, and dropping ``previous`` lowers the VIF of the other two variables of "
"the previous campaign."
msgstr "常见的经验法则把 VIF 高于 5（或高于 10）视为有害的共线性。这里所有的值都远低于这一水平；剔除 ``previous`` 后，另外两个描述上一次营销活动的变量的 VIF 也随之降低。"

msgid "Logistic regression on WOE"
msgstr "基于 WOE 的逻辑回归"

msgid ""
"``logistic_regression`` fits the model with an intercept and reports each coefficient with its "
"standard error, its Wald z statistic and the two-sided p-value of that statistic. A model with a "
"single WOE-encoded variable shows why WOE suits a logistic regression:"
msgstr ""
"``logistic_regression`` 拟合带截距项的模型，并报告每个系数及其标准误、Wald z 统计量和该统计量的双侧 p 值。只含一个 WOE 编码变量的模型说明了 WOE "
"为什么适合逻辑回归："

msgid ""
"kivi defines the WOE of a group as :math:`\\ln(p_i / q_i)`, the log of its share of events over "
"its share of non-events. That equals the log odds of the group minus the log odds of the whole "
"sample, so an intercept equal to the sample log odds and a coefficient of 1 reproduce the log "
"odds of every group exactly. The coefficient is exactly 1 whenever no cell needed smoothing."
msgstr ""
"kivi 将分组的 WOE 定义为 :math:`\\ln(p_i / q_i)` "
"，即其事件占比与非事件占比之比的对数。它等于该组的对数优势减去整个样本的对数优势，因此截距取样本的对数优势、系数取 1，就能精确重现每个组的对数优势。只要没有单元格需要平滑，系数就恰好为 1。"

msgid ""
"With several variables, each coefficient weighs a variable against the others. A higher WOE "
"always means a higher event rate, so every coefficient should be positive. A negative one means "
"that the other variables reverse the variable's effect, usually because of collinearity. In the "
"model with every candidate, ``previous`` gets a negative coefficient:"
msgstr ""
"有多个变量时，每个系数衡量的是一个变量相对于其他变量的权重。WOE "
"越高总是意味着事件率越高，所以每个系数都应为正。负系数表示其他变量反转了该变量的作用，通常源于共线性。在包含全部候选变量的模型中， ``previous`` 的系数为负："

msgid ""
"A scorecard built on that model would give fewer points to customers with more previous contacts,"
" although they subscribe more often."
msgstr "基于这个模型的评分卡会给此前联系次数更多的客户更低的分数，尽管他们的认购率更高。"

msgid "Stepwise selection"
msgstr "逐步回归"

msgid ""
"``stepwise`` selects the variables of the model by their p-values. With the default "
"``direction=\"both\"``, it starts from the intercept alone and repeatedly adds the variable with "
"the smallest p-value below ``p_enter`` (0.05), then removes any selected variable whose p-value "
"has risen above ``p_remove`` (0.10). ``direction=\"forward\"`` only adds variables and "
"``direction=\"backward\"`` starts from every variable and only removes them."
msgstr ""
"``stepwise`` 按 p 值筛选模型的变量。默认的 ``direction=\"both\"`` 从只含截距的模型开始，反复加入 p 值最小且低于 ``p_enter`` "
"（0.05）的变量，然后移除 p 值已升至 ``p_remove`` （0.10）以上的已选变量。 ``direction=\"forward\"`` 只加入变量； "
"``direction=\"backward\"`` 则从全部变量开始，只移除变量。"

msgid "``education`` and ``campaign`` were left out because their p-values stay above 0.05."
msgstr "``education`` 和 ``campaign`` 的 p 值始终高于 0.05，因此未入选。"

msgid ""
"By default, ``positive=True`` keeps every coefficient positive: a variable enters only if all "
"coefficients of the extended model are positive, and a variable whose coefficient is not positive"
" is removed first. Here ``previous`` fails on its p-value anyway. With lenient levels it would "
"pass the p-value test, and only the sign rule keeps it out:"
msgstr ""
"默认的 ``positive=True`` 使每个系数都为正：只有扩展后模型的所有系数都为正时变量才会入选，系数不为正的变量会被优先移除。这里 ``previous`` 本来就因 p "
"值而未能入选。若放宽显著性水平，它能通过 p 值检验，只有符号规则会把它排除在外："

msgid ""
"Stepwise selection tests many models on the same data, so the p-values of the selected model are "
"optimistic. Treat the result as a proposal: review each variable with the business, and check the"
" model on a validation sample before using it."
msgstr "逐步回归在同一份数据上检验了许多模型，因此所选模型的 p 值偏乐观。请把结果当作建议：与业务方逐一审核变量，并在使用前用验证样本检验模型。"

msgid ""
"A scorecard must group and encode every variable in the same way in development, validation and "
"production. ``fit_spec`` bins all the columns of a development sample in one call and measures "
"the WOE of every group. The resulting ``BinningSpec`` groups and encodes any other sample with "
"the same edges and WOE values. It can be saved as JSON and loaded again in production without "
"changing the groups or the encoding."
msgstr ""
"评分卡在开发、验证和生产中必须以同样的方式对每个变量分组和编码。 ``fit_spec`` 一次调用即可对开发样本的所有列分箱，并计算每个分组的 WOE。得到的 ``BinningSpec`` "
"用同样的边界和 WOE 值对任意其他样本分组和编码。它可以保存为 JSON，并在生产环境中重新加载，且不会改变分组和编码。"

msgid ""
"Each column is fitted with the functions of :doc:`binning` and :doc:`woe_iv`, so a column of the "
"specification has exactly the edges and table that those steps give it alone."
msgstr "每一列都用 :doc:`binning` 和 :doc:`woe_iv` 中的函数拟合，因此分箱方案中某一列的边界和 WOE 表，与单独对该列执行这些步骤的结果完全相同。"

msgid "Screen the candidates"
msgstr "筛选候选变量"

msgid ""
"With the defaults, every numeric column gets five quantile bins and every other column keeps its "
"labels. The information value of each column gives a first ranking. A warning names each column "
"whose tied quantiles leave fewer bins than requested:"
msgstr "使用默认设置时，每个数值列分为五个等频箱，其他列保留其标签。各列的信息值给出初步排序。如果重合的分位数使某一列的箱数少于期望值，警告会指明该列："

msgid ""
"``quick.tables`` maps each column to its ``woe_table`` result. The columns of ``frame`` are "
"fitted unless ``columns`` names some of them. Leave the target out: ``fit_spec`` raises an error "
"if a column has the name of the ``target`` series."
msgstr ""
"``quick.tables`` 把每一列映射到其 ``woe_table`` 结果。除非 ``columns`` 指定了部分列，否则会拟合 ``frame`` "
"的所有列。请排除目标变量：如果某一列与 ``target`` Series 同名， ``fit_spec`` 会引发错误。"

msgid ""
"Which columns are binned depends on their dtype. Numeric columns, apart from booleans, are "
"binned; columns of any other dtype, such as strings, categories or booleans, keep their labels as"
" groups. To keep integer codes as labels, convert the column to the ``category`` dtype before "
"fitting. A column of dtype ``object`` that holds only numbers raises a warning, because each "
"distinct number would become a group; convert it with ``pandas.to_numeric`` to bin it."
msgstr ""
"哪些列会被分箱取决于其 dtype。数值列（布尔列除外）会被分箱；其他 dtype 的列（例如字符串、类别或布尔列）以其标签作为分组。若要把整数编码当作标签，请在拟合前把该列转换为 "
"``category`` dtype。只含数值的 ``object`` dtype 列会引发警告，因为每个不同的数值都会各成一组；若要对其分箱，请用 ``pandas.to_numeric`` "
"转换。"

msgid "Choose the binning of each column"
msgstr "为每一列选择分箱方式"

msgid ""
"``method``, ``bins``, ``special`` and ``options`` can each be a dict by column. Here ``balance`` "
"is merged until its WOE is monotonic, ``pdays`` is split by a decision tree with the ``-1`` code "
"(\"not contacted before\") in its own group, and ``age`` gets policy bands. A list of edges in "
"``bins`` is used as given; it must run from ``-inf`` to ``inf``, so that every future value falls"
" into a bin:"
msgstr ""
"``method`` 、 ``bins`` 、 ``special`` 和 ``options`` 都可以是按列的 dict。这里 ``balance`` 合并到 WOE 单调为止， "
"``pdays`` 用决策树切分，并让 ``-1`` 编码（“之前未联系过”）单独成组， ``age`` 使用政策分段。 ``bins`` 中的边界列表按原样使用；它必须从 ``-inf`` "
"延伸到 ``inf`` ，以确保之后的任何取值都能落入某个箱："

msgid ""
"Special codes must be numbers, and infinite values must be special codes, as in ``bin_edges``. "
"The methods are ``\"quantile\"`` and ``\"uniform\"`` for ``bin_edges`` and ``\"chimerge\"``, "
"``\"tree\"`` and ``\"monotonic\"`` for the supervised functions. ``bins`` is passed as ``bins`` "
"to ``bin_edges`` and as ``max_bins`` to the others, and ``options`` holds their remaining "
"arguments, such as ``alpha`` or ``min_bin_share``. ``\"monotonic\"`` uses the ``smoothing`` of "
"the specification, so its trend holds in the tables. ``weights`` passes sample weights to every "
"binning function and to ``woe_table``."
msgstr ""
"特殊值编码必须是数值，无穷值必须作为特殊值传入，与 ``bin_edges`` 相同。方法 ``\"quantile\"`` 和 ``\"uniform\"`` 对应 ``bin_edges``"
" ， ``\"chimerge\"`` 、 ``\"tree\"`` 和 ``\"monotonic\"`` 对应有监督分箱函数。 ``bins`` 作为 ``bins`` 传给 "
"``bin_edges`` ，作为 ``max_bins`` 传给其他函数； ``options`` 存放它们的其余参数，例如 ``alpha`` 或 ``min_bin_share`` 。 "
"``\"monotonic\"`` 使用分箱方案的 ``smoothing`` ，因此其单调趋势在 WOE 表中同样成立。 ``weights`` 把样本权重传给每个分箱函数和 "
"``woe_table`` 。"

msgid ""
"``fit_spec`` never re-bins a column on its own. The legacy ``WOEBatch`` lowered the number of "
"bins until the WOE was monotonic; here the method and its options decide, and a column that "
"should be monotonic is fitted with ``\"monotonic\"``."
msgstr ""
"``fit_spec`` 从不自行重新分箱。旧版的 ``WOEBatch`` 会不断减少箱数，直到 WOE 单调；这里由方法及其选项决定，需要单调的列请用 ``\"monotonic\"`` "
"拟合。"

msgid "Group and encode a sample"
msgstr "对样本分组和编码"

msgid ""
"``cut`` groups every column of a sample, and ``woe_transform`` replaces each group with its WOE. "
"Both return the columns of the specification in its order, with the index of the sample:"
msgstr "``cut`` 对样本的每一列分组， ``woe_transform`` 把每个分组替换为其 WOE。二者都按分箱方案的顺序返回其中的列，索引与样本相同："

msgid ""
"A column fitted as numeric must have a numeric dtype in every sample. Read as strings, the code "
"``\"-1\"`` would miss its special group, so ``cut`` and ``woe_transform`` raise an error instead;"
" convert such a column with ``pandas.to_numeric``:"
msgstr ""
"按数值列拟合的列在每个样本中都必须是数值 dtype。如果按字符串读入，编码 ``\"-1\"`` 就无法匹配其特殊值分组，因此 ``cut`` 和 ``woe_transform`` "
"会引发错误；请用 ``pandas.to_numeric`` 转换这样的列："

msgid ""
"A value whose group is not in its column's table, such as a new category, raises an error by "
"default, so it never turns into a silent NaN:"
msgstr "分组不在该列 WOE 表中的取值（例如新类别）默认会引发错误，因此不会悄无声息地变成 NaN："

msgid ""
"The ``unseen`` argument of ``fit_spec`` sets a WOE for such values, for all columns or by column."
" The same holds for a special code or an interval that has no development observations, and for "
"missing values when the development sample had none. A specification is immutable, so change the "
"policy of a fitted one with ``dataclasses.replace``:"
msgstr ""
"``fit_spec`` 的 ``unseen`` 参数为这类取值指定 "
"WOE，可以对所有列统一指定，也可以按列指定。开发样本中没有观测值的特殊值或区间，以及开发样本没有缺失值时的缺失值，也同样处理。分箱方案不可变，因此请用 "
"``dataclasses.replace`` 修改已拟合方案的策略："

msgid "Keep the model variables"
msgstr "保留模型变量"

msgid ""
"After variable selection, keep only the variables of the model before saving the specification "
"for production:"
msgstr "完成变量筛选后，在为生产环境保存分箱方案之前，只保留模型中的变量："

msgid "``production.tables`` can be passed to ``points_table`` as it is; see :doc:`scorecard`."
msgstr "``production.tables`` 可以直接传给 ``points_table`` ；参见 :doc:`scorecard` 。"

msgid "Save and load a specification"
msgstr "保存和加载分箱方案"

msgid ""
"``to_json`` writes the specification as JSON text, and ``from_json`` reads it back into an equal "
"specification that groups and encodes every sample identically. Two specifications are equal when"
" their JSON text is the same, which includes the version of kivi that fitted them:"
msgstr ""
"``to_json`` 把分箱方案写成 JSON 文本， ``from_json`` 将其读回为相等的分箱方案，对每个样本的分组和编码完全相同。两个分箱方案的 JSON "
"文本相同时二者相等，文本中包含拟合它们的 kivi 版本："

msgid ""
"The same specification always gives the same text, so it can be kept under version control and "
"compared. Labels are written as they are, including non-ASCII ones, so save the text as UTF-8:"
msgstr "同一个分箱方案总是得到相同的文本，因此可以纳入版本控制并相互比较。标签按原样写出（包括非 ASCII 标签），因此请以 UTF-8 保存文本："

msgid "``to_dict`` gives the same content as a dict. Each column is one entry of ``variables``:"
msgstr "``to_dict`` 以 dict 给出相同的内容。每一列是 ``variables`` 中的一项："

msgid "The format"
msgstr "格式"

msgid "Key"
msgstr "键"

msgid "Content"
msgstr "内容"

msgid "``format``"
msgstr "``format``"

msgid "Always ``\"kivi.BinningSpec\"``."
msgstr "始终为 ``\"kivi.BinningSpec\"`` 。"

msgid "``format_version``"
msgstr "``format_version``"

msgid ""
"Version of the format, currently 1. A file with a newer version raises an error that asks for a "
"newer kivi, instead of being read in part."
msgstr "格式的版本，目前为 1。版本更新的文件会引发错误，提示升级 kivi，而不会只读取其中一部分。"

msgid "``kivi_version``"
msgstr "``kivi_version``"

msgid "Version of kivi that fitted the specification."
msgstr "拟合该分箱方案的 kivi 版本。"

msgid "``smoothing``"
msgstr "``smoothing``"

msgid "Smoothing of the WOE tables."
msgstr "WOE 表的平滑参数。"

msgid "``variables``"
msgstr "``variables``"

msgid ""
"One entry per column, in order, with ``name``, ``kind`` (``\"numeric\"`` or ``\"categorical\"``),"
" ``unseen`` (``\"raise\"`` or a number) and ``table``, plus ``edges`` and ``special`` for numeric"
" columns."
msgstr ""
"每列一项，按顺序排列，包含 ``name`` 、 ``kind`` （ ``\"numeric\"`` 或 ``\"categorical\"`` ）、 ``unseen`` （ "
"``\"raise\"`` 或数值）和 ``table`` ，数值列另有 ``edges`` 和 ``special`` 。"

msgid "``table``"
msgstr "``table``"

msgid ""
"One entry per group with its label ``bin`` and the columns of ``woe_table``. An interval of a "
"numeric column is written with the two exact edges that bound it."
msgstr "每个分组一项，包含其标签 ``bin`` 和 ``woe_table`` 的各列。数值列的区间用界定它的两个精确边界写出。"

msgid ""
"JSON has no infinite numbers and does not keep the types of labels apart in every language, so "
"labels and edges are written as follows:"
msgstr "JSON 没有无穷数值，在某些语言中也无法区分标签的类型，因此标签和边界按以下方式写出："

msgid "Value"
msgstr "取值"

msgid "JSON"
msgstr "JSON"

msgid "Strings, integers and booleans"
msgstr "字符串、整数和布尔值"

msgid "As they are: ``\"yes\"``, ``1``, ``true``."
msgstr "按原样写出： ``\"yes\"`` 、 ``1`` 、 ``true`` 。"

msgid "Floats"
msgstr "浮点数"

msgid "With a decimal point or an exponent, such as ``1.0``, so that they stay apart from integers."
msgstr "带小数点或指数，例如 ``1.0`` ，以便与整数区分。"

msgid "Infinite numbers"
msgstr "无穷数值"

#, python-brace-format
msgid "``{\"float\": \"inf\"}`` and ``{\"float\": \"-inf\"}``."
msgstr "``{\"float\": \"inf\"}`` 和 ``{\"float\": \"-inf\"}`` 。"

msgid "Intervals"
msgstr "区间"

#, python-brace-format
msgid "``{\"interval\": [left, right], \"closed\": \"right\"}``."
msgstr "``{\"interval\": [left, right], \"closed\": \"right\"}`` 。"

msgid "The missing group"
msgstr "缺失组"

msgid "``null``."
msgstr "``null`` 。"

msgid ""
"Labels of categorical columns must be strings, integers, floats, booleans or intervals; "
"``fit_spec`` rejects other labels, such as dates. ``from_json`` checks every value and rejects "
"``NaN`` or ``Infinity`` in the text, so a damaged file fails with a message instead of encoding "
"wrong values."
msgstr ""
"类别列的标签必须是字符串、整数、浮点数、布尔值或区间； ``fit_spec`` 会拒绝其他标签，例如日期。 ``from_json`` 会检查每个值，并拒绝文本中的 ``NaN`` 或 "
"``Infinity`` ，因此损坏的文件会报错，而不会编码出错误的值。"

msgid ""
"The interval labels of a table are those of ``pandas.cut``, which rounds their bounds for "
"display. The file writes each interval of a numeric column with its two exact edges instead, and "
"``from_json`` turns them back into the labels of ``pandas.cut``:"
msgstr ""
"表中的区间标签来自 ``pandas.cut`` ，其边界为便于显示而经过舍入。文件改用两个精确边界写出数值列的每个区间， ``from_json`` 再把它们还原为 "
"``pandas.cut`` 的标签："

msgid ""
"Software outside kivi that reads the file should bin with ``edges``, match ``special`` codes "
"before intervals as :func:`kivi.binning.cut` does, and find the row of each interval by its two "
"edges. An interval without development observations has no row. Intervals are closed on the "
"right, so ``-inf`` falls into no interval, and ``woe_transform`` treats it as unseen."
msgstr ""
"在 kivi 之外读取该文件的软件应使用 ``edges`` 分箱，像 :func:`kivi.binning.cut` 一样先匹配 ``special`` "
"编码再匹配区间，并按两个边界找到每个区间对应的行。开发样本中没有观测值的区间没有对应的行。区间为左开右闭，因此 ``-inf`` 不落入任何区间， ``woe_transform`` "
"把它视为未见分组。"

msgid ""
"A scorecard ranks applicants; a credit strategy decides whom to approve. :mod:`kivi.strategy` "
"supports the decisions that follow: ``cutoff_table`` shows what each candidate cut-off approves "
"and how many bad outcomes it lets through, ``swap_set`` compares the decisions of a current and a"
" new score, and ``expected_loss`` and ``expected_loss_table`` turn PDs, LGDs and exposures into "
"the expected loss of each applicant and of each grade."
msgstr ""
"评分卡对申请人排序，信贷策略决定通过哪些申请人。:mod:`kivi.strategy` 支撑随后的决策：``cutoff_table`` "
"显示每个候选截断点通过哪些申请人、放进多少坏结果，``swap_set`` 比较现行评分与新评分的决策，``expected_loss`` 和 ``expected_loss_table`` 将"
" PD、LGD 和敞口转换为每个申请人和每个等级的预期损失。"

msgid "Score direction and the approval rule"
msgstr "评分方向与通过规则"

msgid ""
"As in :doc:`metrics`, every score is higher for a higher risk, such as a PD. An applicant is "
"approved when the score is at or below the cut-off, so a higher cut-off approves more applicants."
" A score equal to the cut-off is approved, and tied scores therefore always get the same "
"decision."
msgstr ""
"与 :doc:`metrics` 相同，所有评分都是风险越高、评分越高，例如 "
"PD。评分不高于截断点的申请人予以通过，因此截断点越高，通过的申请人越多。等于截断点的评分予以通过，所以相同评分总是得到相同的决策。"

msgid ""
"Scorecard points run the other way: a policy that approves 600 points or more approves the "
"applicants whose negated points are at most -600. Pass ``-points`` and the negated cut-offs, for "
"example ``cutoff_table(-points, target, cutoffs=[-620, -600, -580])``."
msgstr ""
"评分卡分数方向相反：通过 600 分及以上的策略，等于通过取负分数不超过 -600 的申请人。请传入 ``-points`` 和取负后的截断点，例如 "
"``cutoff_table(-points, target, cutoffs=[-620, -600, -580])`` 。"

msgid "PDs of two scorecards"
msgstr "两张评分卡的 PD"

msgid ""
"The examples on this page use the bundled bank data. The data record a marketing response rather "
"than a default, so read target 1 as a default, as in :doc:`scorecard`. The first 3,000 rows are "
"the development sample and the remaining 1,521 rows stand for the applicants of a later period. "
"Two logistic regressions on WOE values give the PDs of a current scorecard with four variables "
"and of a new one that adds ``loan`` and ``marital``:"
msgstr ""
"本页示例使用内置的银行数据。该数据记录的是营销响应而非违约，因此与 :doc:`scorecard` 一样，将目标值 1 视为违约。前 3,000 行为开发样本，其余 1,521 "
"行代表后一时期的申请人。基于 WOE 值的两个逻辑回归分别给出现行评分卡（四个变量）和新评分卡（增加 ``loan`` 和 ``marital`` ）的 PD："

msgid "The new scorecard ranks the applicants a little better:"
msgstr "新评分卡对申请人的排序略好一些："

msgid "Choosing a cut-off"
msgstr "选择截断点"

msgid ""
"``cutoff_table`` takes the candidate cut-offs and reports, for each, the approved book and what "
"the cut-off rejects. A PD of 1 approves everyone and gives the reference row:"
msgstr "``cutoff_table`` 接收候选截断点，并对每个截断点报告通过客群以及被拒绝的部分。PD 为 1 的截断点通过所有人，给出参照行："

#, python-format
msgid ""
"Each row is a possible policy. A cut-off of 0.10 approves 784 of the 1,521 applicants, 51.5%, and"
" their bad rate of 6.25% is about half the 11.4% of all applicants. It avoids 71.7% of the bad "
"outcomes, but also turns away 45.5% of the good applicants. Raising the cut-off to 0.15 approves "
"87.4% at a bad rate of 8.3%: the lender gains volume and accepts more risk. Which row to choose "
"is a business decision; the table shows its price."
msgstr ""
"每一行都是一种可能的策略。截断点 0.10 通过 1,521 名申请人中的 784 名，即 51.5%，其坏账率为 6.25%，约为全部申请人 11.4% 的一半。它避开了 71.7% "
"的坏结果，但也拒绝了 45.5% 的好申请人。将截断点提高到 0.15，通过率为 87.4%，坏账率为 "
"8.3%：放款机构获得了更多业务量，也承担了更多风险。选择哪一行是业务决策，表中给出了每种选择的代价。"

msgid "``approved``"
msgstr "``approved``"

msgid "Applicants with a score at or below the cut-off."
msgstr "评分不高于截断点的申请人数。"

msgid "``approval_rate``"
msgstr "``approval_rate``"

msgid "Share of all applicants that the cut-off approves."
msgstr "截断点通过的申请人占全部申请人的比例。"

msgid "``approved_event``, ``approved_event_rate``"
msgstr "``approved_event``, ``approved_event_rate``"

msgid "Events among the approved applicants and their rate, the bad rate of the approved book."
msgstr "通过的申请人中的事件数及其比率，即通过客群的坏账率。"

msgid "``rejected_event_share``"
msgstr "``rejected_event_share``"

msgid "Share of all events with a score above the cut-off: the bad outcomes the cut-off avoids."
msgstr "评分高于截断点的事件占全部事件的比例，即该截断点避开的坏结果。"

msgid "``rejected_non_event_share``"
msgstr "``rejected_non_event_share``"

msgid "Share of all non-events with a score above the cut-off: the good business the cut-off gives up."
msgstr "评分高于截断点的非事件占全部非事件的比例，即该截断点放弃的好业务。"

msgid "``approved_loss``"
msgstr "``approved_loss``"

msgid "With ``loss``, the sum of the losses of the approved applicants; see below."
msgstr "传入 ``loss`` 时，通过的申请人的损失之和；见下文。"

msgid ""
"The bad rate of the approved book averages over everyone approved. The cut-off itself is better "
"judged by the marginal bad rate, the bad rate of the applicants that a higher cut-off adds:"
msgstr "通过客群的坏账率是对所有通过者的平均。评判截断点本身，更适合看边际坏账率，即提高截断点后新增申请人的坏账率："

msgid ""
"Suppose a good loan earns a margin :math:`m` and a bad loan loses :math:`L`. A group of "
"applicants with bad rate :math:`b` earns :math:`(1 - b)\\,m - b L`, which is positive while "
":math:`b < m / (m + L)`. With a margin of 1 and a loss of 10 the break-even bad rate is "
":math:`1/11 \\approx 9.1\\%`. The applicants between 0.05 and 0.08 default at 5.6% and pay for "
"themselves, while those between 0.08 and 0.10 default at 10.4% and do not, so 0.08 is the most "
"profitable of these cut-offs. For a well-calibrated PD the break-even rate is itself the PD cut-"
"off; the marginal rates check it against the observed outcomes."
msgstr ""
"假设一笔好贷款赚取利润 :math:`m`，一笔坏贷款损失 :math:`L`。坏账率为 :math:`b` 的一组申请人带来 :math:`(1 - b)\\,m - b L` 的收益，当 "
":math:`b < m / (m + L)` 时为正。利润为 1、损失为 10 时，盈亏平衡坏账率为 :math:`1/11 \\approx 9.1\\%`。PD 在 0.05 到 0.08"
" 之间的申请人违约率为 5.6%，能够覆盖自身的损失；而 0.08 到 0.10 之间的申请人违约率为 10.4%，无法覆盖，因此在这些截断点中 0.08 的利润最高。对于校准良好的 "
"PD，盈亏平衡坏账率本身就是 PD 截断点；边际坏账率则用实际结果对其加以检验。"

msgid ""
"An integer ``cutoffs`` places the cut-offs at the quantile edges of ``bin_edges``, so that the "
"rows approve about a fifth, two fifths and so on of the applicants. Tied scores move the steps, "
"because all applicants with the same score get the same decision:"
msgstr ""
"整数 ``cutoffs`` 将截断点放在 ``bin_edges`` "
"的分位数边界上，使各行大约通过五分之一、五分之二……的申请人。相同评分会使各级的位置偏移，因为评分相同的申请人总是得到相同的决策："

msgid "Swap sets"
msgstr "交换集"

msgid ""
"A new score changes the decisions of some applicants. At the cut-offs of both scores, "
"``swap_set`` sorts the applicants into four groups: those both scores approve, the swap-outs that"
" only the current score approves, the swap-ins that only the new score approves, and those both "
"decline. To compare the scores at the same approval rate, give the new score the cut-off that "
"approves as many applicants as the current cut-off of 0.10:"
msgstr ""
"新评分会改变部分申请人的决策。在两个评分各自的截断点上，``swap_set`` 将申请人分为四组：两个评分都通过的、只有现行评分通过的换出（swap-out）、只有新评分通过的换入（swap-"
"in），以及两个评分都拒绝的。为了在相同通过率下比较两个评分，给新评分设定一个截断点，使其通过的申请人数与现行截断点 0.10 相同："

msgid ""
"The new score swaps out 105 applicants with a bad rate of 15.2% and swaps in 118 with a bad rate "
"of 6.8%. Because of tied scores, its cut-off approves 797 applicants, 13 more than the current "
"one, and the bad rate of the approved book falls from 6.25% to 5.1%:"
msgstr ""
"新评分换出 105 名坏账率为 15.2% 的申请人，换入 118 名坏账率为 6.8% 的申请人。由于存在相同评分，其截断点通过 797 名申请人，比现行截断点多 13 名，通过客群的坏账率从"
" 6.25% 降至 5.1%："

msgid ""
"A new score is worth adopting when its swap-ins are better than its swap-outs; the applicants "
"both scores approve or decline do not change. The row shares give the approval rate of each "
"score, for example ``swaps[\"share\"].xs(\"approve\", level=\"new\").sum()`` for the new one."
msgstr ""
"当换入优于换出时，新评分才值得采用；两个评分都通过或都拒绝的申请人不受影响。各行的比例给出每个评分的通过率，例如新评分的通过率为 "
"``swaps[\"share\"].xs(\"approve\", level=\"new\").sum()`` 。"

msgid ""
"In practice the outcomes of the swap-ins are unknown: the current score declined them, so they "
"never received a loan. Pass a target with missing values for unknown outcomes. They count in "
"``total`` and ``share`` but not in ``known``, ``event`` and ``event_rate``:"
msgstr ""
"实际上，换入申请人的结果是未知的：现行评分拒绝了他们，所以他们从未获得贷款。对结果未知的申请人，在目标值中传入缺失值。他们计入 ``total`` 和 ``share``，但不计入 "
"``known``、``event`` 和 ``event_rate``："

msgid ""
"The swap-outs are known, but the bad rate of the swap-ins is missing, and with it half of the "
"comparison. Reject inference estimates the outcomes of declined applicants from their scores and "
"the outcomes of similar approved ones. Pass the inferred labels, or the augmented sample with its"
" weights, to fill in the table, and treat the result as an estimate: it depends on the "
"assumptions of the inference."
msgstr "换出申请人的结果已知，但换入申请人的坏账率缺失，比较也就缺了一半。拒绝推断根据被拒申请人的评分和相似的已通过申请人的结果，估计被拒申请人的结果。传入推断得到的标签，或带权重的扩充样本，即可补全该表；但应把结果视为估计值，它取决于推断所依据的假设。"

msgid "Expected loss"
msgstr "预期损失"

msgid ""
"The expected loss of an exposure is the product of its probability of default, its loss given "
"default and its exposure at default:"
msgstr "一笔敞口的预期损失是其违约概率、违约损失率与违约风险敞口的乘积："

#, python-format
msgid ""
"The bank data have no loan amounts, so the examples take the average balance as the exposure, "
"with negative balances set to zero, and one LGD of 45% for all applicants. ``expected_loss`` "
"accepts one value or one per applicant for the LGD and the EAD, and keeps the index of a Series:"
msgstr ""
"银行数据中没有贷款金额，因此示例以平均余额作为敞口，负余额记为零，所有申请人的 LGD 均取 45%。``expected_loss`` 的 LGD 和 EAD "
"可以是一个值，也可以每个申请人一个值，并保留 Series 的索引："

msgid ""
"Pass the expected losses as ``loss`` to ``cutoff_table`` to add the expected loss of the approved"
" book:"
msgstr "将预期损失作为 ``loss`` 传给 ``cutoff_table``，即可加入通过客群的预期损失："

msgid ""
"Approving everyone carries an expected loss of 125,487, or 82.50 per applicant. A cut-off of 0.10"
" approves half of the applicants and only a fifth of that expected loss, 35.26 per approved "
"applicant. ``approved_loss`` adds up whatever is passed as ``loss``: pass realized losses to see "
"the losses each cut-off lets through, whose difference from the last row is the loss it avoids, "
"or pass the exposures to see the volume it approves."
msgstr ""
"通过所有人时，预期损失为 125,487，即每名申请人 82.50。截断点 0.10 通过一半申请人，预期损失却只有其五分之一，即每名通过的申请人 35.26。``approved_loss``"
" 对作为 ``loss`` 传入的任何金额求和：传入实际损失，可看到每个截断点放进来的损失，它与最后一行之差就是该截断点避开的损失；传入敞口，可看到它通过的业务量。"

msgid "Expected loss by grade"
msgstr "按等级的预期损失"

msgid ""
"``expected_loss_table`` adds up the exposures and expected losses of each grade or other group. "
"Cut the PDs of the new score at the edges of a master scale, as in :doc:`calibration`:"
msgstr "``expected_loss_table`` 汇总每个等级或其他分组的敞口和预期损失。与 :doc:`calibration` 一样，按主标尺的边界切分新评分的 PD："

#, python-format
msgid ""
"The expected loss rate, expected loss divided by exposure, rises from 1.7% in grade A to 29% in "
"grade F. With one LGD for everyone it is the LGD times the exposure-weighted PD; with an LGD per "
"applicant it also reflects the collateral of each grade. The rows follow the grades of the scale,"
" as in ``calibration_table``, and grades without applicants are left out."
msgstr ""
"预期损失率即预期损失除以敞口，从 A 级的 1.7% 上升到 F 级的 29%。所有人使用同一 LGD 时，它等于 LGD 乘以按敞口加权的 PD；每个申请人有各自的 LGD "
"时，它还反映了各等级的担保情况。与 ``calibration_table`` 一样，各行按标尺的等级排列，没有申请人的等级不列出。"

msgid ""
"The portfolio totals are the sums of the columns, and its expected loss rate is the ratio of two "
"sums:"
msgstr "组合的合计是各列之和，其预期损失率是两个和之比："

msgid ""
"Comparing each grade's share of the exposure with its share of the expected loss shows where the "
"losses concentrate:"
msgstr "比较每个等级在敞口中的占比与在预期损失中的占比，可以看出损失集中在哪里："

#, python-format
msgid ""
"Grades E and F hold under a tenth of the exposure but almost 30% of the expected loss. A policy "
"that declines grade F, a PD above 0.4, gives up 2.7% of the exposure and avoids 14.4% of the "
"expected loss; the price of those loans would otherwise have to cover a loss rate of 29%."
msgstr ""
"E 级和 F 级的敞口不到十分之一，却占预期损失的近 30%。拒绝 F 级（PD 高于 0.4）的策略放弃 2.7% 的敞口，避开 14.4% 的预期损失；否则这些贷款的定价就必须覆盖 29% "
"的损失率。"

msgid ""
"``cutoff_table``, ``swap_set`` and ``expected_loss_table`` take ``weights``, one non-negative "
"weight per applicant, as the functions of :mod:`kivi.metrics` do. Counts, exposures and losses "
"become sums of weights, and integer weights give the same counts and sums as repeating rows. For "
"``cutoff_table`` this holds on explicit cut-offs: an integer ``cutoffs`` uses the weighted "
"quantiles of ``bin_edges``, which can differ from the quantiles of repeated rows. Use the weights"
" of an outcome-based sample, which keeps all bad outcomes but only some of the good ones, to "
"report approval and bad rates for the whole population."
msgstr ""
"``cutoff_table``、``swap_set`` 和 ``expected_loss_table`` 与 :mod:`kivi.metrics` 中的函数一样接受 "
"``weights``，即每个申请人一个非负权重。计数、敞口和损失都变为加权和，整数权重与重复相应行得到的计数和各项和相同。对 ``cutoff_table`` "
"而言，这只在显式截断点上成立：整数 ``cutoffs`` 使用 ``bin_edges`` "
"的加权分位数，可能与重复行的分位数不同。对于保留全部坏结果、只保留部分好结果的按结果抽样样本，使用其权重即可报告整个总体的通过率和坏账率。"

msgid ""
"Once a scorecard is in use, the loans it approves are monitored as they age. :mod:`kivi.vintage` "
"covers the two standard views of a loan portfolio: vintage curves, which follow the bad rate of "
"each origination cohort by month on book, and roll rates and transition matrices, which show how "
"loans move between delinquency buckets from one month end to the next."
msgstr ""
"评分卡投入使用后，需要跟踪其批准的贷款随账龄增长的表现。 :mod:`kivi.vintage` 提供贷款资产组合的两种标准视角：Vintage "
"曲线按账龄跟踪每个放款批次的坏账率；滚动率和转移矩阵展示贷款从一个月末到下一个月末在逾期档位之间的迁移。"

msgid ""
"Both work on a loan panel in long format, with one row per loan and month on book. The examples "
"use the synthetic panel of ``make_loan_panel``: 5,000 instalment loans originated from January "
"2024 to December 2025 and observed at every month end up to January 2026."
msgstr ""
"两者都基于长格式的贷款面板数据，每笔贷款的每个账龄一行。示例使用 ``make_loan_panel`` 生成的合成面板：5,000 笔分期贷款，在 2024 年 1 月至 2025 年 12 "
"月间发放，并在每个月末观测，直到 2026 年 1 月。"

msgid ""
"The status is an ordered categorical of days past due, so a comparison such as "
"``panel[\"status\"] >= \"60-89\"`` follows the order of the buckets. :doc:`datasets` describes "
"how the panel is simulated."
msgstr ""
"状态是按逾期天数排列的有序分类变量，因此像 ``panel[\"status\"] >= \"60-89\"`` 这样的比较会遵循档位的顺序。 :doc:`datasets` "
"介绍了面板的模拟方式。"

msgid "Vintage curves"
msgstr "Vintage 曲线"

msgid ""
"A loan is *ever bad* by month on book :math:`k` if it was bad at any month on book up to "
":math:`k`. A vintage table holds, for each cohort and month on book, the share of the cohort's "
"loans that are ever bad by then. ``vintage_table`` takes the loan, the cohort, the month on book "
"and whether the loan is bad on each row, so the bad definition is a condition on the status. Here"
" a loan is bad once it is 90 days past due:"
msgstr ""
"如果贷款在账龄 :math:`k` 及之前的任一账龄为坏，就称它到账龄 :math:`k` 为止 *曾经为坏* （ever bad）。Vintage "
"表对每个批次和账龄，给出该批次贷款中到该账龄为止曾经为坏的比例。 ``vintage_table`` "
"接受每一行的贷款、批次、账龄以及该贷款是否为坏，因此坏的定义就是状态上的一个条件。这里贷款一旦逾期 90 天即为坏："

msgid "Cumulative 90+ bad rate by month on book for one cohort in each quarter"
msgstr "每个季度取一个批次，按账龄展示 90 天以上逾期的累计坏账率"

msgid "Vintage curves of the cohorts in the table: each curve stops at the cohort's latest month on book."
msgstr "表中各批次的 vintage 曲线：每条曲线止于该批次最新的账龄月。"

msgid ""
"Each row follows one cohort and never decreases from left to right, because a loan that was bad "
"stays counted as bad even if it cures later. The entries a cohort has not reached are NaN, not 0:"
" the 2025-04 cohort is observed up to month on book 9, so its bad rate at month 12 is not known "
"yet. Reading down a column compares the cohorts at the same age, which separates the quality of "
"new lending from the seasoning of the portfolio. The latest value of each cohort mixes the two, "
"because older cohorts have had more time to go bad."
msgstr ""
"每一行跟踪一个批次，从左到右不会递减，因为变坏过的贷款即使之后回到正常，也一直算作坏。批次尚未达到的取值为 NaN，而不是 0：2025-04 批次只观测到账龄 9，因此其账龄 12 "
"的坏账率还不得而知。沿一列向下读，是在相同账龄上比较各批次，从而把新增放款的质量与资产组合的账龄成熟效应区分开。每个批次的最新取值则混合了二者，因为较早的批次有更长的时间变坏。"

msgid ""
"Every cohort here has about 200 loans, so one bad loan moves its rate by half a percentage point."
" Compare small differences only after averaging several cohorts."
msgstr "这里每个批次约有 200 笔贷款，因此一笔坏贷款就会让坏账率变动半个百分点。比较细小的差异前，应先对多个批次取平均。"

msgid "Bad definitions and amounts"
msgstr "坏的定义与金额"

msgid ""
"An earlier bad definition gives an earlier signal. On the ordered status, ``>= \"60-89\"`` counts"
" the loans that reached 60 days past due or worse:"
msgstr "更早的坏定义能更早给出信号。在有序状态上， ``>= \"60-89\"`` 统计逾期达到 60 天或更严重的贷款："

msgid ""
"To weight each loan by the amount lent, pass ``weights``. The table then reports the share of the"
" cohort's amount lent that went to loans that turned bad:"
msgstr "要按放款金额给每笔贷款加权，请传入 ``weights`` 。此时表中报告的是批次放款金额中属于变坏贷款的比例："

msgid ""
"The weight must be the same on every row of a loan, so pass the amount lent rather than the "
"outstanding balance."
msgstr "同一笔贷款每一行的权重必须相同，因此应传入放款金额，而不是剩余余额。"

msgid "Roll rates"
msgstr "滚动率"

msgid ""
"A roll rate is the share of the loans in a delinquency bucket at one month end that are in the "
"next worse bucket at the next month end. To pair each row with the row of the same loan one month"
" on book later, merge the panel with itself shifted by one month. The last row of a loan has no "
"partner, because the loan was repaid or the panel ends, and drops out. Unlike shifting the rows "
"within each loan, the merge pairs the right months however the rows are sorted and wherever a "
"month is missing:"
msgstr "滚动率是某个月末处于某一逾期档位的贷款中，下一个月末处于下一个更差档位的比例。要把每一行与同一笔贷款账龄大一个月的那一行配对，可以把面板与平移一个月后的自身合并。贷款的最后一行没有配对行（因为贷款已还清或面板已结束），会被去掉。与在每笔贷款内部平移各行不同，无论各行如何排序、中间是否缺少某个月，合并都能配对正确的月份："

#, python-format
msgid ""
"Both columns are ordered categoricals, so ``roll_rates`` takes the order of the states, from the "
"best to the worst, from their categories. For plain labels, pass ``states``: sorted, "
"``\"current\"`` would come after ``\"90+\"``. Each month about 2.3% of the current loans miss an "
"instalment, and the share that rolls on rises with the days past due: seven in ten of the loans "
"at 60 to 89 days are 90 days past due a month later."
msgstr ""
"两列都是有序分类变量，因此 ``roll_rates`` 从其类别中获得状态从最好到最差的顺序。对于普通标签，请传入 ``states`` ：如果按排序， ``\"current\"`` 会排在"
" ``\"90+\"`` 之后。每个月约有 2.3% 的正常贷款漏缴期款，且继续滚动的比例随逾期天数增加：逾期 60 到 89 天的贷款中，有七成在一个月后逾期达到 90 天。"

msgid ""
"A loan falls at most one bucket further behind per month, so the only way from current to 90+ in "
"four months is to roll every month. If the movements follow a Markov chain, the product of the "
"roll rates is the share of current loans that are 90+ four months later:"
msgstr "贷款每个月最多再恶化一个档位，因此四个月内从正常到 90+ 的唯一途径是每个月都滚动。如果迁移服从马尔可夫链，各滚动率的乘积就是正常贷款在四个月后处于 90+ 的比例："

msgid "Balance roll rates weight each loan by its balance at the first month end, as loss forecasts do:"
msgstr "余额滚动率按第一个月末的余额给每笔贷款加权，这也是损失预测的做法："

msgid "Transition matrices"
msgstr "转移矩阵"

msgid ""
"``transition_matrix`` shows all the movements, not only the roll to the next bucket. Row ``i``, "
"column ``j`` counts the loans that moved from state ``i`` to state ``j``:"
msgstr "``transition_matrix`` 展示全部迁移，而不只是滚动到下一档位的部分。第 ``i`` 行、第 ``j`` 列统计从状态 ``i`` 迁移到状态 ``j`` 的贷款数："

msgid "With ``normalize=True``, each row holds the shares of its loans and sums to 1:"
msgstr "设置 ``normalize=True`` 后，每一行给出该行贷款的比例，合计为 1："

msgid ""
"The diagonal holds the loans that stayed in their bucket, the ``current`` column the cures and "
"the entries just right of the diagonal the roll rates. A loan that reaches 90+ stays there in "
"this data, so the last row is all 90+."
msgstr "对角线是保持在原档位的贷款， ``current`` 列是回到正常的贷款，紧挨对角线右侧的取值就是滚动率。在这份数据中，到达 90+ 的贷款会一直停留在 90+，因此最后一行全部是 90+。"

msgid "Migration between two dates"
msgstr "两个日期之间的迁移"

msgid ""
"The same function compares any two observations of the same entities, such as the rating grades "
"of obligors at two annual reviews or the delinquency buckets of a portfolio at two month ends. "
"Here are the loans on book at the end of both June and December 2025:"
msgstr "同一个函数可以比较同一批对象的任意两次观测，例如债务人在两次年度复评时的评级，或资产组合在两个月末的逾期档位。下面是 2025 年 6 月末和 12 月末都在账上的贷款："

msgid ""
"Only the loans on book at both month ends are compared. The 226 loans repaid in between, almost "
"all of them current in June, drop out, so the ``current`` row describes the loans that stayed on "
"book. Missing values raise an error instead of being counted, so first decide what to do with the"
" entities observed only once: drop them, as here, or give them a state of their own, such as "
"``\"closed\"``, to keep them in the shares."
msgstr ""
"这里只比较两个月末都在账上的贷款。期间还清的 226 笔贷款（6 月时几乎都是正常状态）被去掉了，因此 ``current`` "
"行描述的是仍在账上的贷款。缺失值会引发错误，而不会被计入，因此请先决定如何处理只被观测到一次的对象：像这里一样删除，或者给它们一个单独的状态，例如 ``\"closed\"`` "
"，使它们保留在比例中。"

msgid ""
"If the monthly movements followed a time-homogeneous Markov chain, the sixth power of the monthly"
" matrix would give the six-month matrix. Comparing the shares that end in 90+ shows how far that "
"holds:"
msgstr "如果月度迁移服从时齐马尔可夫链，月度矩阵的六次幂就会给出六个月的矩阵。比较最终处于 90+ 的比例，可以看出这一假设在多大程度上成立："

msgid ""
"The projection is of the right size but not exact: loans differ in risk, and the chance of "
"missing an instalment depends on the month on book, so the movements are not a time-homogeneous "
"Markov chain. Few loans are 30 to 89 days past due in June, so those rows are also uncertain."
msgstr "推算值的量级正确，但并不精确：贷款的风险各不相同，且漏缴期款的概率取决于账龄，因此迁移并不是时齐马尔可夫链。6 月逾期 30 到 89 天的贷款很少，因此这些行本身也不确定。"

msgid ""
"``woe_table`` measures how each group separates a binary target. An event is target 1 and a non-"
"event is target 0. Both target classes must be present. Group and target series must share the "
"same index; arrays and lists are matched by position."
msgstr "``woe_table`` 衡量每组对二分类目标的区分能力。标签 1 表示事件，0 表示非事件。数据须同时包含两类标签。分组与标签序列的索引必须相同；数组和列表按位置对应。"

msgid ""
"For group :math:`i`, let :math:`E_i` and :math:`N_i` be its numbers of events and non-events. Its"
" shares of all events and of all non-events are"
msgstr "对第 :math:`i` 组，令 :math:`E_i` 和 :math:`N_i` 分别为其事件数和非事件数。它在全部事件和全部非事件中的占比为"

#, python-brace-format
msgid "p_i = \\frac{E_i}{\\sum_j E_j}, \\qquad q_i = \\frac{N_i}{\\sum_j N_j}."
msgstr "p_i = \\frac{E_i}{\\sum_j E_j}, \\qquad q_i = \\frac{N_i}{\\sum_j N_j}."

msgid "The weight of evidence and the information value contribution of the group are"
msgstr "该组的证据权重和信息值贡献为"

msgid ""
"A positive WOE means that the group is relatively more common among events. Each IV contribution "
"is zero or positive, because :math:`p_i - q_i` and :math:`\\ln(p_i / q_i)` always share a sign."
msgstr "WOE 为正表示该组在事件中相对更常见。每组的 IV 贡献都大于或等于零，因为 :math:`p_i - q_i` 与 :math:`\\ln(p_i / q_i)` 的符号始终相同。"

msgid ""
"Two thirds of group ``a`` are events and two thirds of group ``b`` are non-events, so the two "
"groups have opposite WOE values of :math:`\\pm\\ln 2`."
msgstr "组 ``a`` 中三分之二是事件，组 ``b`` 中三分之二是非事件，因此两组的 WOE 互为相反数，等于 :math:`\\pm\\ln 2`。"

msgid ""
"The first columns describe each group on its own: its counts, its share of all observations and "
"its event rate."
msgstr "前几列描述每组本身：计数、占全部观测的比例和事件率。"

msgid "The remaining columns compare the two classes:"
msgstr "其余各列比较两个类别："

msgid ""
"When the counts are already aggregated, for example from a database query, ``woe`` and ``iv`` "
"take the event and non-event counts of each group and give the same values:"
msgstr "如果计数已经汇总（例如来自数据库查询），可以把每组的事件数和非事件数传给 ``woe`` 和 ``iv`` ，得到相同的结果："

msgid "Smoothing empty cells"
msgstr "空单元格的平滑"

msgid ""
"A group without events or without non-events would have an infinite WOE. Before the shares are "
"computed, each zero count is replaced by the ``smoothing`` value :math:`s`:"
msgstr "没有事件或没有非事件的组，其 WOE 会是无穷。计算占比前，每个零计数都会被替换为 ``smoothing`` 参数值 :math:`s`："

#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"\\tilde E_i = \\begin{cases} E_i & E_i > 0 \\\\ s & E_i = 0 \\end{cases}, \\qquad\n"
"p_i = \\frac{\\tilde E_i}{\\sum_j \\tilde E_j},"
msgstr ""
"\\tilde E_i = \\begin{cases} E_i & E_i > 0 \\\\ s & E_i = 0 \\end{cases}, \\qquad\n"
"p_i = \\frac{\\tilde E_i}{\\sum_j \\tilde E_j},"

msgid ""
"and likewise for non-events. Smoothing replaces zero cells with 0.5 by default. Each column is "
"then normalized separately. Counts in the result always report observations."
msgstr "非事件同理。平滑默认用 0.5 替换零频数，再按列分别归一化。结果表中的计数始终是实际观测数。"

msgid ""
"Changing smoothing can materially change the result for sparse bins. Merge small bins, or compare"
" several smoothing values, before relying on their WOE."
msgstr "修改平滑参数可能显著改变稀疏分箱的结果。在依赖这些箱的 WOE 之前，请合并小箱，或比较多个平滑取值的结果。"

msgid "``non_event_share``, ``event_share``"
msgstr "``non_event_share``, ``event_share``"

msgid "``total_share``"
msgstr "``total_share``"

msgid "The group's share of all observations, without smoothing."
msgstr "该组占全部观测的比例，不做平滑。"

msgid ""
"Events divided by the total of the group, without smoothing. For a default target this is the bad"
" rate."
msgstr "该组事件数除以该组总数，不做平滑。当目标为违约时，即为坏账率。"

msgid "``woe``"
msgstr "``woe``"

msgid ":math:`\\ln(p_i / q_i)`."
msgstr ":math:`\\ln(p_i / q_i)`."

msgid "``iv``"
msgstr "``iv``"

msgid "The group's IV contribution. Sum the column for the variable's IV."
msgstr "该组的 IV 贡献。对该列求和得到变量的 IV。"

msgid ""
"A widely used rule of thumb reads an IV below 0.02 as not predictive, 0.02 to 0.1 as weak, 0.1 to"
" 0.3 as medium and above 0.3 as strong. Treat these bands as a starting point, not as a test; a "
"very high IV often points to a leak of the target into the variable."
msgstr ""
"一种广泛使用的经验口径是：IV 低于 0.02 视为无预测力，0.02 到 0.1 为弱，0.1 到 0.3 为中等，高于 0.3 为强。这些区间只是参考起点，而非检验标准；IV "
"过高往往意味着目标信息泄漏到了该变量中。"

msgid "Charting WOE"
msgstr "绘制 WOE 图"

msgid ""
"A WOE chart is the usual way to review a variable with the business: the share of customers and "
"the event rate of each group on top, the WOE below. Categorical variables read best when sorted "
"by WOE."
msgstr "WOE 图是与业务方一起评审变量的常用方式：上图为每组的客户占比和事件率，下图为 WOE。类别变量按 WOE 排序后最易阅读。"

msgid "Share of customers, subscription rate and WOE for each job"
msgstr "每种职业的客户占比、认购率和 WOE"

#, python-format
msgid ""
"WOE by job. Students and retired customers subscribe far more often than blue-collar workers, but"
" students are only 2% of the sample, so their WOE rests on few customers."
msgstr "按职业的 WOE。学生和退休客户的认购率远高于蓝领工人，但学生只占样本的 2%，其 WOE 依赖的客户很少。"

msgid "Plotting code"
msgstr "绘图代码"

msgid ""
"The documentation draws its WOE charts with this matplotlib function. It takes a ``woe_table`` "
"result."
msgstr "本文档用下面这个 matplotlib 函数绘制 WOE 图，它接收 ``woe_table`` 的结果。"

msgid "To compare many variables at once, rank them by IV; see :doc:`risk_workflow`."
msgstr "要同时比较多个变量，可以按 IV 排序，见 :doc:`risk_workflow`。"

msgid "Encoding new data"
msgstr "对新数据编码"

msgid ""
"A scorecard model takes WOE values as inputs. ``woe_transform`` replaces each group with its WOE "
"from a development table, so the validation sample and later production data are encoded with "
"exactly the same values. Group every sample with the edges fitted on the development sample:"
msgstr ""
"评分卡模型以 WOE 值作为输入。 ``woe_transform`` 用开发样本表中的 WOE "
"替换每个分组，因此验证样本和之后的生产数据都会使用完全相同的编码。请用在开发样本上拟合的边界为每个样本分组："

msgid ""
"The result keeps the index of the groups. A missing value takes the WOE of the missing group when"
" the development sample had missing values."
msgstr "结果保留分组的索引。如果开发样本中有缺失值，缺失值会取缺失组的 WOE。"

msgid ""
"A group that is not in the table, such as a category that appears only in later data, raises an "
"error by default, so a mapping problem cannot go unnoticed:"
msgstr "不在表中的分组（例如只在后来的数据中出现的类别）默认会引发错误，因此映射问题不会被忽略："

msgid ""
"Pass ``unseen`` to give such groups a WOE instead. A WOE of 0 is the neutral choice: it stands "
"for the event rate of the whole development sample."
msgstr "也可以传入 ``unseen`` 为这类分组指定 WOE。WOE 为 0 是中性的选择：它代表整个开发样本的事件率。"

msgid ""
"Development samples are often stratified: every bad account is kept, but only a fraction of the "
"good ones. Pass the inverse of each observation's sampling rate as ``weights`` so that the counts"
" describe the population. Below, the sample keeps every subscriber and every fourth other "
"customer, so each non-subscriber stands for four customers."
msgstr ""
"开发样本常常是分层抽样得到的：保留全部坏账户，但只保留一部分好账户。把每个观测抽样比例的倒数作为 ``weights`` "
"传入，计数就能反映总体。下面的样本保留了全部认购客户和每四个其他客户中的一个，因此每个未认购客户代表四个客户。"

msgid ""
"The unweighted sample overstates the event rate, and the weights bring it back to the population "
"level. The WOE does not change, because it compares shares within each class and the weights of a"
" class scale all of its counts alike. That holds while no group is empty in either class: "
"``smoothing`` replaces an empty cell in units of weight, so with weights that do not sum to the "
"number of observations, scale ``smoothing`` along with them. In a weighted result the counts are "
"sums of weights, and groups whose weights sum to zero are left out; ``woe_transform`` treats them"
" as unseen."
msgstr ""
"不加权的样本高估了事件率，加权后事件率回到总体水平。WOE "
"不变，因为它比较的是事件与非事件各自内部的占比，而同一目标类别的权重会使其所有计数按相同比例缩放。前提是没有任何组在某一目标类别中为空： ``smoothing`` "
"以权重为单位替换空单元格，因此当权重总和不等于观测数时，请按相同比例缩放 ``smoothing`` 。加权结果中的计数为权重之和，权重之和为零的组会被排除， ``woe_transform``"
" 会把它们视为未见过的分组。"

